{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts","id":1116730,"title":"Solars starting the game with Artifacts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-15T22:15:45-07:00","id":1116730,"title":"Solars starting the game with Artifacts","content":"I asked about whether Arms of the Chosen will touch on this in the developer thread, but I'm curious what people's experience at their own table has been. It's easy enough to justify the personal arsenal of starting Dynast PCs, or Deathknights, or Sidereals. Even the Lunars, though they have less infrastructure than those, have the Silver Pact which might specifically pass on something that belonged to the PC's previous incarnation, or receive a gift from a mentor, etc.<br /> <br /> What about Solars though? Plenty of character concepts call for starting the game with your signature daiklaive, or powerbow, etc. But how do you narratively explain how a brand new Solar came into the possession of such an artifact? Does everyone just go with &quot;visions led you to the tomb of your First Age incarnation&quot;, or have you found more diverse answers to the question?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T22:54:43-07:00","id":1116735,"title":"","content":"I've had people who were given their golden weapons and arms by a 'mysterious traveler who knew many things'. Basically just a Gold Faction Sidereal who was sitting on a dead Solar's stuff and waiting to give it back when a new incarnation showed up. Also, a few players in my games just stole their starting artifacts from other gods/Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T23:23:30-07:00","id":1116743,"title":"","content":"Got it from a tomb. Stole it. Killed somebody for it. Found it on an expedition.<br /> <br /> The usual places you find them, just your Solar did it off-screen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T00:14:00-07:00","id":1116750,"title":"","content":"My past incarnation stored it in the elsewhere in a cache egg. I was able to summon it to me and then the cache egg shattered. <br /> <br /> My past incarnation asked a god to hold onto it and give it to his next incarnation. He found me and gave it to me. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","name":"WalkingEye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T00:22:22-07:00","id":1116752,"title":"","content":"If you specifically want your previous incarnation's daiklaive, you of course have to find some way for it to have come back to your character . . . but with the reported 3rd edition/Arms approach to magical materials, it's perfectly reasonable that a Usurpation Dragon-Blooded took your incarnation's weapon and gave it to his son, and then after the Great Contagion it was dug up from his grandson's grave and used by a succession of outcastes and exigents and (maybe) God-Blooded until you took it from the rogue who was using it last, or found the hidden treasure trove of bandits slain a century ago.<br /> <br /> If you don't care about it having been yours, well, everything's wide open. After all, your Solar can use any magical material, so any lost daikalive from any origin could be the one you managed to get your hands on.<br /> <br /> Back in 2nd, it was convenient that the Dragon Kings had orichalcum as a favored material. Even if they only &quot;rarely&quot; used it, there were originally 150 million Dragon Kings, of whom about a quarter would have been Raptok with their human-like hands and human-scaled tools and weapons; orichalcum weapons of Raptok extinguished fighting the Primordials could potentially be found anywhere. Of course, that origin is still viable origin for your character's weapon, even if we're now rather hazier on how many Raptok there would have been; perhaps a sinkhole that opened up near his home exposed one that's been buried for thousands of years in the mud where it fell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T02:54:35-07:00","id":1116769,"title":"","content":"Remember that chargen Solars have been Exalted for up to a year. That's plenty of time for background adventures, any of which might put a daiklave in your hands or armour on your shoulders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T03:50:32-07:00","id":1116782,"title":"","content":"Artifacts in my game have largely been granted to the PCs, on either a permanent or temporary basis, by powerful beings for doing some important task. Or occasionally taken off a foe's corpse.<br /> <br /> In fact, none have been the result of finding one's First Age tomb.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T03:51:29-07:00","id":1116783,"title":"","content":"Yeah, mine took hers from a Demon-Blooded would-be warlord, whom she slew when she was Chosen. It can be pretty much anything, depending on what the needs of your story are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>All that I write but don't cite is simply my perspective, colored by my experiences and beliefs. I extrapolate a lot, too, so don't take it too seriously. :P","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7858-end","name":"*End","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7858_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T05:04:01-07:00","id":1116805,"title":"","content":"In 2e I was fond of the fact that Short Daiklaves were stated to be small enough to be used as ordinary swords because as much as Exalted likes its oversized signature weapons I have a soft spot for the idea of taking an old sword to Deckard Cain in order to learn its true properties. On that note I'd also welcome the Horadric Cube.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T05:22:37-07:00","id":1116809,"title":"","content":"In the game I'm DM:ing, the scene where one of the players exalted at the same time as he unlocked the secret containing an old sword was the culmination of the first phase of a decades old conspiracy between mortals, gods and exalted, that started in the back-alleys of yu-shan <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1920-kim","name":"Kim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T06:10:50-07:00","id":1116821,"title":"","content":"There's a couple of situations, but most of them will boil down to:<br /> <br /> A) Looted from a battle pre-story<br /> B) Found in a tomb/ equivalent.<br /> <br /> The most original approach I've seen is a PC in an edited (even more xenphobic) version of Gethamane. There's an academy where scavenged artifacts are studied for mortal uses. One of the un-used Artifact was a very small essence weapon, that the PC studied for her end-of-studies report, and Exalted during those studies (she's Craft-heavy, you see). She had to run because shenanigans, and kept the weapon.<br /> <br /> Oh, and there's always the old &quot;amnesiac with an unknown weapon&quot; standby.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3657-sagara","name":"Sagara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3657_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T07:06:47-07:00","id":1116831,"title":"","content":"And I created a character with artifact armour and four different weapons: daiklave, powerbow, infinite chakram, and smashfists, justified as the greatest treasures of the house to which she was a retainer, taken at the order of the Lady of the house to keep them from their enemies' hands when the house fell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T09:45:27-07:00","id":1116868,"title":"","content":"That's something a bit different, I like it.<br /> <br /> I've always been a fan of the old &quot;there was a daiklaive stuck in a rock and only the Chosen One can pull it out&quot;. And you did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T09:46:46-07:00","id":1116869,"title":"","content":"In addition to the stuff mentioned already (I particularly like &quot;artifact passed knowingly or unknowingly down a family line&quot;), I'm a big fan of mundane objects ascending to Artifact status without any intentional (re)forging process, and Exaltation is as good of an example of the very special circumstances necessary for that to happen as any. Plus, with all the Artifacts forged in the lost mists of yonks ago, a &quot;newborn&quot; one provides some interesting counter-play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/396-mr-rage","name":"Mr Rage","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T09:53:49-07:00","id":1116872,"title":"","content":"Well if it's jade, a simple 'took it from some DB who attacked you for being anathema' works.<br /> <br /> For orichalcum, one idea I've had but not used is an ancient artifact kept as a ceremonial sacred weapon for a remote tribe, said to have been wielded by some mythic hero in ages past. Cue a young warrior of the tribe who one day starts glowing gold picking it up and wielding it, hailed as said hero born again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 07-16-2017, 01:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T09:57:28-07:00","id":1116873,"title":"","content":"That's also much easier now that Solars suffer no penalties for having jade weaponry.<br /> <br /> It also leads to more interesting plot I feel (though that of course is subjective).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T18:51:07-07:00","id":1117037,"title":"","content":"i have a supernal crafter who forged his artifact in a moment of desperate inspiration and need to protect others upon exalting","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <div align=\"left\">Elemental and dragon line descriptors and capturing device coming soon</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1131843-my-own-take-on-a-craft-rewrite-that-inclu\" target=\"_blank\">Craft Rewrite </a> W/ Points, Slots, and Charms</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1106793-2nd-circle-demon-c-al-siphar-soc-initiation-symbiosis-of-the-burning-heart-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Demon Adversaries and Related Sorcerous Initiation</a></div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1091536-seeking-thoughts-and-suggestions-on-constructing-an-organization-in-game-specifically-a-university\" target=\"_blank\">Executive Leadership</a> Organization Merrit</div> <hr /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1990-norraba","name":"norraba","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1990_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T19:11:43-07:00","id":1117041,"title":"","content":"Conversely, there's not much really stopping the Dragon Blooded from carrying Artifacts made from everything else.<br /> <br /> Even soulsteel is good for those who aren't concerned with not getting the full power out of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T19:59:22-07:00","id":1117064,"title":"","content":"A couple times already my solar started with it by nearly drowning and finding it in a pocket of air in some cave or temple underwater.<br /> One just happened to start the game with Summoning the Loyal Steel, and lo' there was a sword there!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T07:53:21-07:00","id":1117192,"title":"","content":"As a ST, I having the characters being from seconds after they exalted, up to a few weeks since they exalted, as the the game started. The idea is to let the players get used to the system (2.5-ish) as the characters get used to their powers. During char-gen, I have informed them that we either have to come up with some explanation of why they have what they have; or they will get it somehow during one of the early game sessions (this isn't limited to artifacts, but also to resources, allies, familiars, etc).<br /> <br /> So when it comes to artifacts picked during char-gen, there has been...<br /> From before the game started:<br /> * Family heirloom the character nabbed while running away.<br /> * From a heist a couple of days before exalting.<br /> * An item given by the character's tribe after exalting, as the character was pushed into a position/rank of the tribe (well, that one was more an important piece for a manse not already having access to).<br /> <br /> After the game started:<br /> * Placed in a show-case, in a hidden manse guarded by a huge demonic guardian, during the first session. The character being able to deactivate and reactivate the defense system, and the creature welcoming the character back, and informing the contract is now fulfilled, before going poof (beside the two artifacts, the player had put some points into having a manse).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T09:17:10-07:00","id":1117237,"title":"","content":"Based on a misread of second ed, my headcanon states that when a solar dies, all objects in Elsewhere remain in Elsewhere, accessible by the Solar's next incarnation. As long as some other schmuck didn't pull out the blade between you and the first age, that five-dot artifact is sitting in Elsewhere just waiting for you dramatic Exaltation. Gives players the artifacts they want with no fuss.<br /> <br /> Additionally, if &quot;but five-dot artifacts at char gen!&quot; is your thing, then fine, the manse that powers it is broken. You have to fix it before it becomes four dot, and then you need a wargod's blessing (attuned motes!) to make it five dot. Because I'm all about fun and balance, and this is fun and balanced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T09:33:16-07:00","id":1117245,"title":"","content":"I find the most common explanation in the myriad of groups I've been in is &quot;stolen from the scarlet dynasty.&quot; Either spoils of a killed Wyld Hunt, stolen prize out of the heptagram, snapped up during a daring raid of the imperial palace, stuff like that.<br /> <br /> Oddly I've never even seen somebody who got it from his former incarnations tomb.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T10:28:35-07:00","id":1117273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1117041#post1117041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conversely, there's not much really stopping the Dragon Blooded from carrying Artifacts made from everything else.<br /> <br /> Even soulsteel is good for those who aren't concerned with not getting the full power out of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about &quot;good&quot;. It's made of souls after all. It's existence is against the Immaculate Philosophy. What to do with Soulsteel swords has been an occasional moral dilemma I've seen faced by DBs in games.<br /> None of them came up with great answers to free the souls, but they never used them in battle at least (unlike Lunar PCs).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 07-17-2017, 01:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T10:47:05-07:00","id":1117278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1117273#post1117273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's existence is against the Immaculate Philosophy.</div> </div> </div> </div>In what way? A ghost's existence is already a defiance of doctrine; confining it in a way that makes it useful to Dragon-Blooded is better than leaving it to cause trouble, yes?<br /> <br /> (Also, even DBs raised from birth with the Immaculate Philosophy can be more pragmatic about it.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-17-2017, 01:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T10:56:59-07:00","id":1117282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Childofthesun1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1117237#post1117237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm all about fun and balance</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bBy screwing around with people's Merits before the game even starts?<br /> <br /> Bad form.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is made of souls after all. It is existence is against the Immaculate Philosophy.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bHmm, that might raise a question about how widely the nature of soulsteel is, but that's probably a bit arbitrary.<br /> <br /> \u200bRegardless, even assuming Dragon Blooded who adhere to the philosophy, there are liable to be some who are a bit lax on the particulars, as there are with any religion.<br /> <br /> \u200bIn any case, the soulsteel Artifact in the core was once carried by a Sesus.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T11:13:11-07:00","id":1117296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Childofthesun1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1117237#post1117237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Additionally, if &quot;but five-dot artifacts at char gen!&quot; is your thing, then fine, the manse that powers it is broken. You have to fix it before it becomes four dot, and then you need a wargod's blessing (attuned motes!) to make it five dot. Because I'm all about fun and balance, and this is fun and balanced.</div> </div> </div> </div>My way to handle it, is if they pick something that will need a lot of work, so it isn't worth the points spent in its current form, it will be worth a lot more when it is fixed. So those three dot spent on an artifact, that currently is a glorified paperweight, probably is at least a five dot one when fixed.<br /> <br /> But, I'm not really concerned with balance in the first place. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T11:33:25-07:00","id":1117309,"title":"","content":"Artifacts, particularly weapons, are weird because the game wants them to be fabled weapons of legend all, with storied histories and pedigrees similar to champion racehorses, while simultaneously wanting every Solar to be able to trip over a half dozen of them within seconds of Exalting so they can pick out the exact one that\u2019s absolutely perfect for them, personally.<br /> <br /> For myself, I generally started imposing a limit on the number of starting Artifact dots based on how much effort I felt the player put into describing how they acquired them. \u201cI found it in my Solar tomb\u201d would get you a single dot, going up from there. Three dots was a hard limit for any one Artifact, unless accompanied by sufficient backstory and bribery (typically dice and pizza).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T11:39:32-07:00","id":1117319,"title":"","content":"I think when Isator Levi said soul steel was &quot;good,&quot; for a Dragon-Blooded he meant &quot;a valid choice,&quot; not &quot;desirable&quot; or &quot;morally sound.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T11:53:09-07:00","id":1117343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Childofthesun1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1117237#post1117237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Additionally, if &quot;but five-dot artifacts at char gen!&quot; is your thing, then fine, the manse that powers it is broken.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:9px\">\u200bOkay, bit of revision to remove some of the salt:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u200bThinking more about this, I have to ask: what's the point of that when an Essence 1 character can only get one or two Evocations out of the thing in the first place? In the sample Artifacts we've gotten, Evocations dependent on things like manse power sources, being fed 100 souls, or soothing the demon inside of them tend to be the pinnacle, which aren't accessible until Essence 4 or 5.</span></span><br /> <br /> \u200bUnless you're proposing that the Artifact that they paid good character creation points for is not one to which they are entitled so much as a single Evocation. Which is to say, the single Evocation that they would be able to use anyway.<br /> <br /> \u200bI don't know, maybe that Lore Charm, Wake the Sleeper, is assumed to let one buy Evocations even without the Essence minimum? Personally, I would find that to be a case in which it is assumed not to unless explicitly stated otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T12:05:18-07:00","id":1117353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1117309#post1117309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Artifacts, particularly weapons, are weird because the game wants them to be fabled weapons of legend all, with storied histories and pedigrees similar to champion racehorses, while simultaneously wanting every Solar to be able to trip over a half dozen of them within seconds of Exalting so they can pick out the exact one that\u2019s absolutely perfect for them, personally.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bHmm, now I'm curious to go back over example Solars who were never meant to be playable and seeing how many of them have Artifacts, because the whole time with this thread I've been thinking about the point that the idea of people getting their weapons from the tombs of their past lives being a common thing for players to do doesn't mean that it is a common thing in the setting.<br /> <br /> \u200bNo matter how many groups describe that as part of the background for their own characters in their own game, it doesn't need to mean that every one of those characters is not the first person to do it in the world, because these games are not taking place in a shared universe.<br /> <br /> \u200bHow many games involve people defeating or taking over the Realm? That doesn't make the Realm a kind of ultra concentrated ghost kingdom.<br /> <br /> \u200bEven accounting for that, there are still some faults in the logic, from either end. On the one hand, something being commonly associated with people who are themselves rarer than hens teeth doesn't exactly make those things common. Quite a few monarchs have been in possession of jewel-encrusted gold crowns, and yet these things are not cheap trinkets. Crowns that, incidentally, often have distinct appearances and names and stories to them. Rare people and rare things going hand in hand doesn't exactly make them less rare.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe other side to it is the fallacy of assuming that a thing being merely uncommon (as opposed to extremely rare) doesn't mean that it can't be unique with an interesting story to it.<br /> <br /> I mean, champion racehorses? How many of those do you think there are?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For myself, I generally started imposing a limit on the number of starting Artifact dots based on how much effort I felt the player put into describing how they acquired them. \u201cI found it in my Solar tomb\u201d would get you a single dot, going up from there. Three dots was a hard limit for any one Artifact, unless accompanied by sufficient backstory and bribery (typically dice and pizza).</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat just sounds awful. Arbitrarily acting as a gatekeeper to people engaging with the game unless they satisfy some kind of pre-game creative writing challenge?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T14:29:53-07:00","id":1117438,"title":"","content":"Just realized another reason for me to like the &quot;semi-sentient seeking missile shards&quot; I'm going with when I ST.<br /> <br /> I can explain away why so many Lunars and Solars are lucky in already having access to those artifacts, by the shards often looking for qualified people in proximity of those items. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T14:44:58-07:00","id":1117450,"title":"","content":"When I ST, I usually house-rule that no player can start with more than a 3-dot artifact<br /> <br /> If anyone asks why not more, then.... &quot;Your tomb was looted of all the good stuff, its lost to time, deal with it&quot;<br /> <br /> 4 and 5 dot artifacts from the getgo... good grief no. A singing staff, maybe - but IIRC then word of god would have that it should probably have been a 3 dot artifact anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T15:15:54-07:00","id":1117467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1117438#post1117438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just realized another reason for me to like the &quot;semi-sentient seeking missile shards&quot; I'm going with when I ST.<br /> <br /> I can explain away why so many Lunars and Solars are lucky in already having access to those artifacts, by the shards often looking for qualified people in proximity of those items. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bBecause telling whether or not there's a nearby daiklave is beyond the power of the Unconquered Sun?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T15:48:31-07:00","id":1117482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1117467#post1117467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bBecause telling whether or not there's a nearby daiklave is beyond the power of the Unconquered Sun?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I thought the want for Sol to pick his chosen himself was to have some deeper meaning than &quot;well, you where close to a cool sword while doing something I thought was awsome.&quot; But sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T16:27:56-07:00","id":1117497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1117309#post1117309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For myself, I generally started imposing a limit on the number of starting Artifact dots based on how much effort I felt the player put into describing how they acquired them. \u201cI found it in my Solar tomb\u201d would get you a single dot, going up from there. Three dots was a hard limit for any one Artifact, unless accompanied by sufficient backstory and bribery (typically dice and pizza).</div> </div> </div> </div>I do the same but only when it would kind of mess with the setting/story I'm trying to create. Like if the first adventure or two revolve around traversing the dangerous caravan routes and one guy wants to start with a kireeki class skyreme they need a really good reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T21:11:07-07:00","id":1117583,"title":"","content":"My character's backstory has him picking up the red jade twin daiklaves dropped by the Immaculate he punched into a mast immediately after exalting. I'm waiting for <i>Arms of the Chosen</i> to come out before figuring out what its Evocations are, but they're likely not going to be all that well-suited for a gilled Lintha pirate who's best at swimming over to opponent's ships and climbing aboard under the cover of night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T08:28:14-07:00","id":1117756,"title":"","content":"My players tend toward the &quot;weapon exalts with you&quot; style. The Dawn caste, as a mortal, had a sword that was daiklave sized because he thought it would add to his warrior reputation*. When he Exalted, the blade became part of his legend and incrementally grew in power with him. It became a Major Artifact in our 3ed game (we accidentally unmade the world in our 2.5 game, 3rd is a Universal reboot). The Zenith used his warhammer to kill a powerful shadowlands beast and his weapon became an Artifact because of his intense zeal and puritanical hatred**. The Night found hers in a lost jungle temple. The Twilight and Eclipse didn't use an artifact at start.<br /> <br /> *Like Guts, he trained with a longsword as a child and kept &quot;trading up&quot; in size as he grew. Even though he could barely wield the thing with any control, it was enough to make him a good caravan guard.<br /> <br /> **He had his reinforced with Oricalcum after. Actually, they both did, as raw Oricalcum was a quest reward. <br /> <br /> Personally, when I design a character I never design them as a level 1 scrub, I design them as being good at what their schtick is and compromise as needed with the rule system of the game. The fact that I can start Exalted with my Legendary Weapon and Supernal Skill is a massive draw for me. This isn't DnD with it's ragtag rat-hunters starting quests, you are Living Legends, andhalf of our mythic heroes are inextricably linked with their legendary weapons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T10:56:02-07:00","id":1117846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1117309#post1117309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Artifacts, particularly weapons, are weird because the game wants them to be fabled weapons of legend all, with storied histories and pedigrees similar to champion racehorses, while simultaneously wanting every Solar to be able to trip over a half dozen of them within seconds of Exalting so they can pick out the exact one that\u2019s absolutely perfect for them, personally.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since, fluff-wise, your evocations from a daiklaive are going to be different from my evocations with the same daiklaive (just the same general theme), then I think it's more that whatever daiklaive they pick up is appropriate for them, rather than they find the appropriate daiklaive.<br /> <br /> Unless you're talking about them getting the panoply of their previous incarnation (which, as much as it is a stereotype, I haven't actually seen very much at all in Solar games... or maybe not at all? I don't remember any examples from games I've played/run), in which case the answer is Sidereals.<br /> <br /> You see, Gold-Faction Sidereals are always trying to help Solars meet their destiny (and helping people meet their destiny is what Sidereals do).<br /> Sidereals guide luck and coincidence so 4-6 disparate Solars happen to be in the same town when a massive army of Raksha turn up to duel any local heroes for the souls of the townsfolk, and these 4-6 disparate Solars happen to be the reincarnations of Solars who knew each other in a previous life. And said Sidereals will also help guide them to run into Abyssal villains who were their friends/rivals in a previous life.<br /> And the Sidereals guide them to coincidentally find an ancient tomb of their previous incarnation where they find the destined daiklaive and armour of their previous life.<br /> <br /> In my game, there was a couple of years where every 4-5 months the party's Full Moon would leave and be replaced by another Full Moon even more optimised for combat than the previous one, but with surprisingly similar personalities and reactions to things.<br /> Presumably this is because the Sidereals screwed up and created a fate loop.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T11:03:05-07:00","id":1117850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1117450#post1117450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I ST, I usually house-rule that no player can start with more than a 3-dot artifact<br /> <br /> If anyone asks why not more, then.... &quot;Your tomb was looted of all the good stuff, its lost to time, deal with it&quot;<br /> <br /> 4 and 5 dot artifacts from the getgo... good grief no. A singing staff, maybe - but IIRC then word of god would have that it should probably have been a 3 dot artifact anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll be honest, in Exalted, I've never found any problems with people having level 5 artefacts at the beginning, compared to them having Essence 4 and min-maxed stats (luckily, they can no longer have Essence 4... but they can still take some Essence 5 charms! I find that much more awkward, as an ST, than a level 5 artefact).<br /> Daiklaive of Conquest? The player liked it, but I found it pretty irrelevant (so that was find).<br /> Singing Staff? Yeah, that was fine.<br /> Airship? Worked pretty well, and I hope to see that character return now his replacement is dead, so we can once again fly around together.<br /> <br /> And of course now, things like Level 5 armour or weapons don't matter so much because they have to put a whole bunch of XP into unlocking its full power. Which can be rather OP, but I no way find it as difficult, as an ST, than a Melee Supernal Dawn with 15 melee charms. Now that's the sort of character I really can't cope with at 0xp.<br /> <br /> The only artefacts I think we ever banned with Skinmount Amulets (bloody hell, those things were broken).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T11:04:34-07:00","id":1117851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1117756#post1117756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My players tend toward the &quot;weapon exalts with you&quot; style. The Dawn caste, as a mortal, had a sword that was daiklave sized because he thought it would add to his warrior reputation*. When he Exalted, the blade became part of his legend and incrementally grew in power with him. It became a Major Artifact in our 3ed game (we accidentally unmade the world in our 2.5 game, 3rd is a Universal reboot). The Zenith used his warhammer to kill a powerful shadowlands beast and his weapon became an Artifact because of his intense zeal and puritanical hatred**. The Night found hers in a lost jungle temple. The Twilight and Eclipse didn't use an artifact at start.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now this I like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T11:25:52-07:00","id":1117866,"title":"","content":"Heh, I had an image of somebody decrying the supposed convenience of their being a tomb containing at least one Artifact available for every Solar, when, y'know, the whole reincarnation thing means that every single living Solar (and the ones of ambiguous living status) is going to have at least one tomb with the panoply of one previous life in the world.<br /> <br /> \u200bY'know, [I]maaaybe[I] a daiklave that you got in a tomb is well-suited to you because it belonged to you in five previous lives.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe complaint of almost everybody seeming to have an Artifact contradicting the perception of Artifacts as uncommon seems to be assuming that the main characters of the game are regular people rather than members of a highly exclusive category. It would be something else if you were just playing Conan, where he's just this guy who happened to stumble upon a tomb containing some Atlantean steel, and then kept encountering these other regular people who just happened to have the same experience. The whole being Chosen by God, and these being divine weapons made to be wielded by those Chosen by God kind offff standardises the variables a bit. Also adds a certain aspect of mysticism.<br /> <br /> \u200bLike, the Exalted can experience visions irrespective of past life memories and the workings of Fate, and an uncanny intuition for the location of the final resting place of a previous life might be amongst those, especially if it's housing an ancient mystical weapon that might be really enthusiastic about coming back into your hands that might be very subtly calling out to you.<br /> <br /> \u200bHehehe, how's that for convenience? &quot;Oh, I just happened to stumble upon the tomb of a past life. At least, I assume that I just stumbled upon it, since I didn't consciously decide to do it, and surely all thought processes and decision making are governed consciously rather than having all kinds of unconscious cognitive processes informing, if not outright driving them. Right? That's how brains work, right? You know, 'free will' and all that.&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bIf I was in that position, I'd be a bit inclined to go back over any of the decision making that put me on the path winding up in the tomb to try and identify the point at which I started being compelled towards finding it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T00:04:14-07:00","id":1118095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1117866#post1117866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThe complaint of almost everybody seeming to have an Artifact contradicting the perception of Artifacts as uncommon seems to be assuming that the main characters of the game are regular people rather than members of a highly exclusive category. It would be something else if you were just playing Conan, where he's just this guy who happened to stumble upon a tomb containing some Atlantean steel, and then kept encountering these other regular people who just happened to have the same experience. The whole being Chosen by God, and these being divine weapons made to be wielded by those Chosen by God kind offff standardises the variables a bit. Also adds a certain aspect of mysticism.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is pretty big, yeah. A lot of people still seem to look at Exalted characters as if they're 1st level D&amp;D adventurers made with the baseline stat arrays or 3d6 in order -- random bumpkins with no connection to the world, no history to them, and no particular significance beyond &quot;is played by a player.&quot;. Just by being an Exalt you're part of an incredibly exclusive category of people, and being a Solar puts you in an even narrower one. Additionally, while anyone can potentially Exalt, in the roughly a year following Exaltation it's assumed you're going to have done stuff, practiced, trained, adventured, etc. That's why you have a 8/6/4, 25 ability points, and 15 bonus points statline, rather than something closer to the Militia statline, whose <b>best</b> rolls are 4-5 dice; if you were a mere conscript or brigand at exaltation you've probably done a lot of stuff and rapidly mastered your newfound talents in the last year.<br /> <br /> Obviously if the game starts with &quot;and suddenly you're goldshiny and have no idea why&quot;, then yeah, you might need to adjust and set artifacts as &quot;Things I hope to find&quot; rather than &quot;things I start gameplay with&quot;, but, &quot;suddenly you're goldshiny and have no idea why&quot; is definitely not standard assumption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T07:24:43-07:00","id":1118159,"title":"","content":"I think a lot off it is also the fact that in other WW games, the PCs start out as scrubs, at least by default. The Solar Exalted are not scrubs, but much of the player base, or rater, much of the ST base, is rather resistant to the idea of a starting character having Cool Stuff simply that 's Not The Way It Is in other games, meaning WoD/CoD/D&amp;D (and its variants). Of course, it doesn't help that in the Exalted setting as written in the prior editions, there are huge incentives for the players to stick to extremely low-profile actions; there's a reason Jon Chung created Jon Chung Exalted (which he despised, by the way); it was a necessary consequence of the rules as written and the setting as presented.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1184,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","user":"LadyLens","date":". 07-19-2017, 11:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T08:40:52-07:00","id":1118182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1117850#post1117850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only artefacts I think we ever banned with Skinmount Amulets (bloody hell, those things were broken).</div> </div> </div> </div>But they're the best","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <div align=\"left\">Elemental and dragon line descriptors and capturing device coming soon</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1131843-my-own-take-on-a-craft-rewrite-that-inclu\" target=\"_blank\">Craft Rewrite </a> W/ Points, Slots, and Charms</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1106793-2nd-circle-demon-c-al-siphar-soc-initiation-symbiosis-of-the-burning-heart-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Demon Adversaries and Related Sorcerous Initiation</a></div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1091536-seeking-thoughts-and-suggestions-on-constructing-an-organization-in-game-specifically-a-university\" target=\"_blank\">Executive Leadership</a> Organization Merrit</div> <hr /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1990-norraba","name":"norraba","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1990_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T08:56:58-07:00","id":1118186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1117353#post1117353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThat just sounds awful. Arbitrarily acting as a gatekeeper to people engaging with the game unless they satisfy some kind of pre-game creative writing challenge?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Or</i> bribery. You completely left that part out.<br /> <br /> And I don't really see it so much as a challenge as putting in a bare minimum of effort. &quot;I found it in my Solar Tomb&quot; is Exalted's &quot;You all meet in the tavern and are given a quest by a mysterious stranger.&quot; It's bog standard and hackneyed, is basically no-effort, and even twisting or subverting the trope in some way carries elements of being trite. Yes, yes, there's nothing new under the sun and all that, but you can at least range more than three feet from the cliche.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1118095#post1118095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is pretty big, yeah. A lot of people still seem to look at Exalted characters as if they're 1st level D&amp;D adventurers made with the baseline stat arrays or 3d6 in order -- ...</div> </div> </div> </div>I know that 3d6 in order gets denigrated pretty heavily, but I really recommend that people do it at least once. I actually find playing a less-than-perfect character incredibly interesting and fun, and even if you end up not liking it than you can at least criticize it from a place of experience.<br /> <br /> GMing a 3d6 game is very interesting too, since you open up a wider range of challenges for the PCs who don't have perfectly assigned and min-maxed (to a greater or lesser extent) stats.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T12:01:38-07:00","id":1118234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1118186#post1118186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>Or</i> bribery. You completely left that part out.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not better.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I don't really see it so much as a challenge as putting in a bare minimum of effort. &quot;I found it in my Solar Tomb&quot; is Exalted's &quot;You all meet in the tavern and are given a quest by a mysterious stranger.&quot; It's bog standard and hackneyed, is basically no-effort, and even twisting or subverting the trope in some way carries elements of being trite. Yes, yes, there's nothing new under the sun and all that, but you can at least range more than three feet from the cliche.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bOr it's an element to the setting that was deliberately put in in the first place to create a straightforward justification for having a panoply with some verisimilitude, so that people could just get on with the game.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs for taverns, well - decades from now, there are going to be games that suggest the backstory for how the group gets together will be that they met on an Internet forum, and there will be snarky individuals who will deride that as a clich\u00e9 because they lack the personal experience of that being an entirely normal way for people to meet. Of it being <i>the</i> way that people used to meet, back before they had telepathy or whatever.<br /> <br /> \u200bSet a game in ancient Byzantium, and you could make it &quot;you all met in the Hippodrome&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T12:22:32-07:00","id":1118238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1118186#post1118186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> you can at least range more than three feet from the cliche.</div> </div> </div> </div>But what if I don't want to? What if, for me, playing the cliche is enjoyable? Am I just disallowed from having my kind of fun at your table? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T12:49:19-07:00","id":1118248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1118186#post1118186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that 3d6 in order gets denigrated pretty heavily, but I really recommend that people do it at least once. I actually find playing a less-than-perfect character incredibly interesting and fun, and even if you end up not liking it than you can at least criticize it from a place of experience.<br /> <br /> GMing a 3d6 game is very interesting too, since you open up a wider range of challenges for the PCs who don't have perfectly assigned and min-maxed (to a greater or lesser extent) stats.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have done it, so I am not speaking from ignorance: It very much depends on what you want out of the game. Often people go into games wanting to play something in particular. Learning that you aren't allowed to play a fighter because your strength is too low is not some sort of character-building disappointment that will make you a better person, it is frustration in your limited free time.<br /> <br /> Every human who has ever lived is familiar with not having &quot;stats&quot; that correspond to what they want for themselves. We all &quot;roleplay&quot; that every single day. It is not bad roleplaying to want to get in the shoes of someone who actually feels important and competent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T14:35:09-07:00","id":1118281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1118238#post1118238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But what if I don't want to? What if, for me, playing the cliche is enjoyable? Am I just disallowed from having my kind of fun at your table?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not directed to you alone, but quoted because it was the best direct text to quote on this particular subtopic.<br /> <br /> Where do this &quot;I should be allowed to do my thing at every gaming group&quot;? Different people have different wants in gaming, which make some compatible, while others not so much. Trying to mix too much, compromising, and no one will be happy.<br /> <br /> There are things disallowed at my table. There are things I want that's disallowed at other peoples tables. A &quot;X? Well, I prefer Y myself&quot; I would understand, but why all these post of complaining about how other people are doing around a table not being a part of?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T15:12:09-07:00","id":1118292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1118186#post1118186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I don't really see it so much as a challenge as putting in a bare minimum of effort. &quot;I found it in my Solar Tomb&quot; is Exalted's &quot;You all meet in the tavern and are given a quest by a mysterious stranger.&quot; It's bog standard and hackneyed</div> </div> </div> </div>Both are pretty much, in my experience, what are referred to on TV Tropes as dead unicorn tropes: regarded as cliche without ever have been common or widespread in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T15:47:50-07:00","id":1118296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1118292#post1118292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both are pretty much, in my experience, what are referred to on TV Tropes as dead unicorn tropes: regarded as cliche without ever have been common or widespread in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can definitely tell you &quot;you all meet in a tavern and are hired for a quest&quot; is a pretty common way to start d&amp;d campaigns for newbies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T16:31:41-07:00","id":1118303,"title":"","content":"What about the idea of &quot;giving&quot; your players random artifacts from the getgo? Like, make a table with all 1 or 2 dot artifacts, roll some dice, and say &quot;Oh and you find this&quot;<br /> <br /> useless random magic crap makes for unpredictable and hilarious gameplay<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T16:32:25-07:00","id":1118304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1118296#post1118296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can definitely tell you &quot;you all meet in a tavern and are hired for a quest&quot; is a pretty common way to start d&amp;d campaigns for newbies.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Exalted version of that is &quot;You meet in Great Forks and some god there hires you for a quest&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T20:08:58-07:00","id":1118383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1118296#post1118296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can definitely tell you &quot;you all meet in a tavern and are hired for a quest&quot; is a pretty common way to start d&amp;d campaigns for newbies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Especially when several of the published adventures start exactly like that. Published adventures seem like an easier way to get your feet wet, though not always as PCs have a remarkable ability to get obsessed with minor details and wander off on random tangents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T20:22:40-07:00","id":1118390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1118248#post1118248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have done it, so I am not speaking from ignorance: It very much depends on what you want out of the game. Often people go into games wanting to play something in particular. Learning that you aren't allowed to play a fighter because your strength is too low is not some sort of character-building disappointment that will make you a better person, it is frustration in your limited free time.<br /> <br /> Every human who has ever lived is familiar with not having &quot;stats&quot; that correspond to what they want for themselves. We all &quot;roleplay&quot; that every single day. It is not bad roleplaying to want to get in the shoes of someone who actually feels important and competent.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Same. Hell, I've played 4d6 7 times drop lowest, or 25-point buy, and still been subject to the same problems I actually cited - random bumpkins with no connection to the world, no history to them, and no particular significance beyond &quot;is played by a player&quot;. Starting with 0 dots of merits/backgrounds, essentially, because at best you have a tab with the local barkeep, not influence over an area or reputation as a powerful warlord or a magic weapon of terrifying power from ages past.<br /> <br /> Exalted, at core, isn't about playing those random bumpkins; even random bumpkin Exalt will either A) not spend all their merit points (an option, but one you are specifically taking rather than having forced upon you by the game's conceits) or B) have some stuff like Mighty Thew, Danger Sense, or Natural Resistance, so as not to have those connections. They'll be special in some way, comparatively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T20:35:30-07:00","id":1118393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1118390#post1118390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Same. Hell, I've played 4d6 7 times drop lowest, or 25-point buy, and still been subject to the same problems I actually cited - random bumpkins with no connection to the world, no history to them, and no particular significance beyond &quot;is played by a player&quot;. Starting with 0 dots of merits/backgrounds, essentially, because at best you have a tab with the local barkeep, not influence over an area or reputation as a powerful warlord or a magic weapon of terrifying power from ages past.<br /> <br /> Exalted, at core, isn't about playing those random bumpkins; even random bumpkin Exalt will either A) not spend all their merit points (an option, but one you are specifically taking rather than having forced upon you by the game's conceits) or B) have some stuff like Mighty Thew, Danger Sense, or Natural Resistance, so as not to have those connections. They'll be special in some way, comparatively.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> also not having access to these merits really limitis the characters naratively wise, like we have a play who is the son of a dynast, there would be no way for him to have that player the way they want and start with zero merits","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <div align=\"left\">Elemental and dragon line descriptors and capturing device coming soon</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1131843-my-own-take-on-a-craft-rewrite-that-inclu\" target=\"_blank\">Craft Rewrite </a> W/ Points, Slots, and Charms</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1106793-2nd-circle-demon-c-al-siphar-soc-initiation-symbiosis-of-the-burning-heart-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Demon Adversaries and Related Sorcerous Initiation</a></div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1091536-seeking-thoughts-and-suggestions-on-constructing-an-organization-in-game-specifically-a-university\" target=\"_blank\">Executive Leadership</a> Organization Merrit</div> <hr /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1990-norraba","name":"norraba","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1990_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T06:13:26-07:00","id":1118501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1118281#post1118281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not directed to you alone, but quoted because it was the best direct text to quote on this particular subtopic.<br /> <br /> Where do this &quot;I should be allowed to do my thing at every gaming group&quot;? Different people have different wants in gaming, which make some compatible, while others not so much. Trying to mix too much, compromising, and no one will be happy.<br /> <br /> There are things disallowed at my table. There are things I want that's disallowed at other peoples tables. A &quot;X? Well, I prefer Y myself&quot; I would understand, but why all these post of complaining about how other people are doing around a table not being a part of?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Don't misunderstand - I'm not saying everything should be allowed at every table. Some things ruin games. Some things are overpowered. Some things make the game not fun for everyone else at the table. But how I got my daiklave doesn't affect anyone else. You might think it's boring. That's fine, think that. But don't tell me <b>I</b> can't do it because <b>you</b> think it's boring. It's bad form, it's stepping on my fun, and it guarantees I won't be coming back to that table. <br /> <br /> My fun is just as important as anyone else's fun at the table (GM's included), and when someone else at the table tells me I can't do what I think is fun just because they think it's too cliche, I walk. I'm sure I'm not the only one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T09:13:32-07:00","id":1118588,"title":"","content":"Most of the time I saw artifacts in my games, they were either heirlooms that nobody really understood (ex: Single-Point style guy had a daiklave said to have been wielded by the school's founder) or just went unexplained. (hearthstone bracers got that treatment a fair bit). Finding the tomb of a former incarnation never really happened.<br /> <br /> Shocking, I know =/","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T11:11:09-07:00","id":1118630,"title":"","content":"TBH, I think my game was the same. I don't think I ever saw people actually turn up with their previous incarnations' stuff.<br /> My favourite explanation was for the street urchin's orichalcum God-Kicking Boots.<br /> &quot;Where did you get those amazing legendary golden boots?&quot;<br /> &quot;Oh, my panther familiar brought them to me one day.&quot;<br /> &quot;Where did he get them?&quot;<br /> &quot;I didn't ask.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> I did, as ST, have people find places belonging to their previous incarnation, but they didn't have daiklaives or anything. And not tombs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T11:18:26-07:00","id":1118635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1118234#post1118234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not better.</div> </div> </div> </div>How is it not better? They get their daiklaive or whatever and I have a new set of dice or a pizza or something. Bribing the GM is a hallowed, time-honored tradition!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1118238#post1118238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But what if I don't want to? What if, for me, playing the cliche is enjoyable? Am I just disallowed from having my kind of fun at your table?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not being disallowed from it. I never said that I <i>disallowed</i> that backstory; if that's seriously what you want to do, you are more than free to put it on record at my table.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1118248#post1118248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have done it, so I am not speaking from ignorance:</div> </div> </div> </div>Kudos. If I wore a hat, it would be off to you. It's probably my bad for just assuming that people bad mouth 3d6 without ever having tried it, but that does seem to be the case more often than not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Learning that you aren't allowed to play a fighter because your strength is too low is not some sort of character-building disappointment that will make you a better person, it is frustration in your limited free time. </div> </div> </div>The last three editions of D&amp;D haven't really had ability minimums, so no worries there. And even in 1e and 2e, you only really need something like a 9 Strength to qualify for fighter. Even if you didn't manage that, I still wouldn't call the character dead. Maybe you're a thief who always wanted to be a fighter; I can think of several interesting angles to work from with that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1118281#post1118281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are things disallowed at my table. There are things I want that's disallowed at other peoples tables. A &quot;X? Well, I prefer Y myself&quot; I would understand, but why all these post of complaining about how other people are doing around a table not being a part of?</div> </div> </div> </div>RPGs, Exalted in particular, are very srs business discussed on teh Intraweb by very srs people who take slaying pretend dragons very srsly. If ideas that they don't like aren't stamped out, then the Council of Ricks and their elite ninja gaming enforcement squad will burst into their dining room and force them to play CHAMPIONS or something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1118292#post1118292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both are pretty much, in my experience, what are referred to on TV Tropes as dead unicorn tropes: regarded as cliche without ever have been common or widespread in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then I suppose that I should start checking my home for an equine that is pointy at one end and poops rainbows from the other, because I've encountered both personally several times. Much to my chagrin I even ran the &quot;you all meet in a tavern&quot; version back in my younger days.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1118303#post1118303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about the idea of &quot;giving&quot; your players random artifacts from the getgo? Like, make a table with all 1 or 2 dot artifacts, roll some dice, and say &quot;Oh and you find this&quot;<br /> <br /> useless random magic crap makes for unpredictable and hilarious gameplay<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I actually rather like the &quot;weird random magic things that may or may not be useful&quot; table that came with 5e. It actually worked out pretty great, since the monk got this weird gear thing, and Mechanus is pretty heavily involved in what I'm doing for this game.<br /> <br /> I also gave the warlock an intelligent <i>wand of wonder</i> with infinite charges, attached to a 5k entry random effect table. He hasn't used it in several sessions, though, because like all sentient magical items the wand is annoying and obnoxious as fuck and he realized that <i>he's</i>, as the caster, the only consistent thing that is a potential target for the wand's effects...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T12:17:06-07:00","id":1118657,"title":"","content":"The only artifacts belonging to past lives I've had have been locked up in said past lives manse (1 might be in atomb, since said past life didn't like having a manse in the first place), and were custom built to reflect the needs of said past life (usually imperfectly aligning with the current life), and took a quest to get.<br /> I usually ask how people _got_ their artifacts, and i've gotten 'from the manse I found' and 'forged for the person people wanted me to be a century ago' respectively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T12:18:36-07:00","id":1118658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1117309#post1117309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For myself, I generally started <b>imposing a limit</b> on the number of starting Artifact dots based on how much effort I felt the player put into describing how they acquired them. \u201cI found it in my Solar tomb\u201d would get you a <b>single dot</b>, going up from there. Three dots was a hard limit for any one Artifact, unless accompanied by sufficient backstory and bribery (typically dice and pizza).</div> </div> </div> </div>Emphases mine. It looks to me, and maybe I'm misinterpreting, that in your game at your table I cannot have a daiklave I found in my Solar tomb. (Without bribery, which is a whole different can of worms.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T13:48:13-07:00","id":1118688,"title":"","content":"While I like a basic background meshing with the things that players put on their character sheets I try not to be a hardass about it. Months or a year as a beginning Solar allows lots of opportunities to upgrade their Merits in impressive ways and the system is designed to allow it. Obviously my tolerance for whats permitted can change with the kind of campaign I'm running. The mortal game I'm running now has completely different degrees of expectations than it would for Exalted Demigods - it made sense that no one had artifacts or manses!.<br /> <br /> As far as justifications I've had everything from 'found in my Solar's tomb' to 'bought in a flea market at a stall of antiquities, unrecognized and waiting' to 'dusty and unused in his grandparent's attic' to 'inherited it from his Lunar mentor' to 'I collected my artifacts off of a Dragon-blooded/God/Sidereal/demon's body'. All these justifications are a bit cliche but they work. I don't need a player to be as creative and witty as Shakespeare for what is essentially background material to fill a paragraph or a few sentences.<br /> <br /> PS: I like encouraging players to pick something other than 'my Solar tomb' because i like those as easy adventures to run for later with suitable personalized rewards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1546,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1546-great-cthulhu","user":"Great Cthulhu","date":". 07-20-2017, 04:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1546-great-cthulhu","name":"Great Cthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1546_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T13:55:21-07:00","id":1118693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1118635#post1118635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is it not better? They get their daiklaive or whatever and I have a new set of dice or a pizza or something. Bribing the GM is a hallowed, time-honored tradition!</div> </div> </div> </div>So you are charging people real money for words on paper when they already spent real money to buy the books, took time to make their characters, and blocked out several hours when they could be doing something else? Because they weren't good enough to pass your creative writing test to your arbitrary standards? Because the fact that they are at the table <i>at all</i> doesn't already show an immense commitment?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1118635#post1118635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The last three editions of D&amp;D haven't really had ability minimums, so no worries there. And even in 1e and 2e, you only really need something like a 9 Strength to qualify for fighter. Even if you didn't manage that, I still wouldn't call the character dead. Maybe you're a thief who always wanted to be a fighter; I can think of several interesting angles to work from with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>A: 3d6 averages 10.5. In any of the last three editions having an 11 in your main stat is the next best thing to worthless. In 3 and 4 it makes you even more dependent on the magic item christmas tree to perform your party role since monster CR was balanced around the heroic array AND the christmas tree. In 5 you are just bad at your job which brings things back to everyone already having experience with roleplaying puny mortals.<br /> <br /> B: In 2E Paladin, Druid, and Bard were basically impossible to ever play. And if you don't have a high enough main stat you can fall even farther behind because other people are getting an xp bonus.<br /> <br /> C: Why should someone have to play a thief who always wanted to be a warrior? Yes, that is a character some people want to play. But if you signed up to play Conan it is unsatisfying because you are being told you aren't allowed to play what you want.<br /> <br /> If the players go in informed and expecting that 3d6 in order is what you are playing that is different. Its basically the same as playing with pregens.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1118635#post1118635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also gave the warlock an intelligent <i>wand of wonder</i> with infinite charges, attached to a 5k entry random effect table. He hasn't used it in several sessions, though, because like all sentient magical items the wand is annoying and obnoxious as fuck and he realized that <i>he's</i>, as the caster, the only consistent thing that is a potential target for the wand's effects...</div> </div> </div> </div>So it is less than worthless and the player appears to have recognized that. Between the possible good/bad/neither results I am going to bet the number that are good are a minority. So to use it in any important situation is a waste of an action at best. Add to the fact that you made it annoying and all you have done is put words on his inventory list that everyone is going to ignore or given them a mcguffin whose properties almost don't matter to be bartered or blown up later. How has this improved anyone's play experience?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 07-20-2017, 05:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T14:11:13-07:00","id":1118697,"title":"","content":"On bribery... I think as a Game Master I've been bribed maybe 2 or 3 times in a long career of running. It was nice, I bent for the player, and kept going. But its not something I'd ever encourage as a regular feature of gaming because it just feels like poor sportsmanship on my part to do so. People are there to have fun, paying out real cash for little fictional bonuses makes the game a bit too serious and contrived, IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1546-great-cthulhu","name":"Great Cthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1546_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T14:30:59-07:00","id":1118702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1118501#post1118501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't misunderstand - I'm not saying everything should be allowed at every table. Some things ruin games. Some things are overpowered. Some things make the game not fun for everyone else at the table. But how I got my daiklave doesn't affect anyone else. You might think it's boring. That's fine, think that. But don't tell me <b>I</b> can't do it because <b>you</b> think it's boring. It's bad form, it's stepping on my fun, and it guarantees I won't be coming back to that table.<br /> <br /> My fun is just as important as anyone else's fun at the table (GM's included), and when someone else at the table tells me I can't do what I think is fun just because they think it's too cliche, I walk. I'm sure I'm not the only one.</div> </div> </div> </div>What ruins a game for someone might be the very thing that makes it worth playing for someone else. Yes, I agree, everyone's fun is equally important. So someones fun on the expense on another player should never be accepted (shared fun on the expense of a character is another thing). Personally I put in quite a bit of effort communicating my expectations, in an attempt to minimize the risk of finding out incompatible wants before anyone gets invested in the game (unfortunately, not always successful).<br /> <br /> I think you should walk away from a game that isn't fitting what you think is fun. If it seems to be worth it, I think it is a good idea to talk it over and see if there is a common ground; but I also see that as something optional. Only you should decide when you might make compromises on your preferences.<br /> <br /> I don't mind cliches myself, but I do mind if it isn't fitting the setting (from that point of view, a cliche is rarely a problem for me). If the reason for an artifact is &quot;I raided my previous life's tomb&quot;, I would want an explanation on why the character didn't get more stuff. Maybe it was already looted and this was the only thing left, maybe was chased off before managing to get anything else, maybe was robbed on the way from there, maybe it was an ad-hoc funeral and this was the only thing that previous life was buried with, etc. When something clashes, I want to figure out what part of it is important to the player (or the ST in the rare occasions I'm the player) and see if there is an alternative that fit both. Still, it matters how a character got its daiklave at my table. It might make us incompatible, or it might not. If we ever are to game together, it would be something we would have to figure out. If we would be incompatible, it wouldn't make anyone right or wrong; just different.<br /> <br /> However, the thing rubbing me the wrong way is all the posts about other people &quot;doing it wrong&quot;. I mean, I wouldn't play at a table where you actually bribe the ST for in-game boons, so if that is what Coik's group is doing, it wouldn't fit me. But if it fit everyone at that table, great for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T14:40:23-07:00","id":1118705,"title":"","content":"I, generally, in the few actually-Exalted campaigns I've run, haven't allowed players to <u>start</u> the game with Artifacts, or, really, <u>any</u> &quot;story'-type merit.<br /> <br /> If you want it, you either gotta play for it, or come up with a damn good <i>story</i> for why you have it. And you had better be ready for me to use your Story-merits in the campaign. If not ..... why do you have it?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T14:58:02-07:00","id":1118713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1118635#post1118635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also gave the warlock an intelligent <i>wand of wonder</i> with infinite charges, attached to a 5k entry random effect table. He hasn't used it in several sessions, though, because like all sentient magical items the wand is annoying and obnoxious as fuck and he realized that <i>he's</i>, as the caster, the only consistent thing that is a potential target for the wand's effects...</div> </div> </div> </div>You absolute evil monster","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T15:06:55-07:00","id":1118719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1118705#post1118705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I, generally, in the few actually-Exalted campaigns I've run, haven't allowed players to <u>start</u> the game with Artifacts, or, really, <u>any</u> &quot;story'-type merit.<br /> <br /> If you want it, you either gotta play for it, or come up with a damn good <i>story</i> for why you have it. And you had better be ready for me to use your Story-merits in the campaign. If not ..... why do you have it?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>What, even resources, influence, stuff like that?<br /> I mean, if you want a game where people start off as poor but heroic, that's fine. It could be quite interesting. It just surprises me.<br /> Hmmm... I think actually I could probably sell my players on that. These days they sometimes miss being hobo-adventurers.<br /> (Actually, we were pleased that 3rd ed lets you buy innate merits like Fleet-Footed or whatever, because several of the players found that concepts like Street Urchin just didn't fit with 7 points of backgrounds in 2nd ed. But then other players will play a local ruler or influential merchant and spend 2-3 dots on followers, resources, influence, backing, and contacts, and find 10 points still isn't enough.)<br /> <br /> <br /> I'll be honest, I don't really get why everyone's so keen on restricting people from taking artefacts. As ST, I find a player with a giant daiklaive and orichalcum light armour is less work than one with Backing 5 or Influence 5.<br /> Though I think requiring people to explain why they have a Daiklaive seems pretty reasonable. Just like you'd expect a PC with Resources to have some reason why (maybe she's a princess, or found a lost treasure hoard, or it's just Resources 2 from her upper-middle class job).<br /> But I don't feel any need to require tons of background; after all, if it's lacking in detail I, as ST, can do stuff with it if I want. And I find that when players are forced to write a whole bunch of background, they come up with dull stuff anyway.<br /> <br /> But then, my players don't take that many artefacts anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 07-20-2017, 06:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T15:36:26-07:00","id":1118725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1118719#post1118719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What, even resources, influence, stuff like that?<br /> I mean, if you want a game where people start off as poor but heroic, that's fine. It could be quite interesting. It just surprises me.<br /> Hmmm... I think actually I could probably sell my players on that. These days they sometimes miss being hobo-adventurers.<br /> (Actually, we were pleased that 3rd ed lets you buy innate merits like Fleet-Footed or whatever, because several of the players found that concepts like Street Urchin just didn't fit with 7 points of backgrounds in 2nd ed. But then other players will play a local ruler or influential merchant and spend 2-3 dots on followers, resources, influence, backing, and contacts, and find 10 points still isn't enough.)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yep.<br /> <br /> If you want Resources, you have to describe it. Describe your business, you land-holdings, your so-on-and-so-forth. That rule comes straight from the book.<br /> <br /> If you want Influence, you have to describe how it works, or how it came about. Why are you so influential in this region?<br /> <br /> If you want Retainers (note that I modified the Retainers merit, so instead of one uberpowerful retainer, you get a larger 'lesser' retinue), you gotta describe where they came from, where you picked them up, how/why you recruited them, why they are loyal to you, so on and so forth.<br /> <br /> If you want Command, you have to describe why the soldiers follow you, and how you keep them supplied.<br /> <br /> If you want Backing..... who backs you, and why? Why are you a member of this organization, who is your superior, how do you feel about each other?<br /> <br /> So on and so forth, for the rest of the Story merits.<br /> <br /> .....perhaps I misspoke. It isn't that I <u>actively dissallow</u> my players from taking Story merits at character creation, it is more that I, well, <i>actually use them in the story</i>. And I prefer to have them gain the Story merits in-play, as a result of their actions, as opposed to just marking things off during character creation.<br /> <br /> For example, let us say Awesome McBadass starts with a Daiklave, looted from his previous incarnation's tomb. So, per the merit, you get your Daiklave...... but, people are going to talk about how <i>someone</i> looted the Anathema MacEvil BigBadEvilGuy's forbidden tomb, braving the dangers within, and escaping with the treasure..... and people are going to ask questions. About how you can carry a blade only the Princes of the Earth can wield, how the hell you survived the place in the first place. Local authority figures are going to be interested, at the very least ...... and depending on how much 'noise&quot; you make looting the joint and surviving the perils, the Wyld Hunt might be called.<br /> <br /> Or..... a Thrifty McMerchant runs a Solar-powered business empire, making beaucoup bucks. Just the Resources merit, right..... but other companies are going to try to make a move on your market, pirates/bandits are going to raid your stuff unless you do something about it, local, or even regional, authority figures are going to try to muscle in on your cash flow, and all the while, resources need to be moved, products need to be produced, and expansion needs to be undertaken.<br /> <br /> All things that, in and of themselves, can, and in my mortal campaigns, often <i>are</i>, stories in and of themselves. In my games, you don't just &quot;get&quot; a merit and mark it down on your character sheet. There are consequences for <i>everything</i>..... not necessarily bad consequences, but things will change, fates will shift, and stuff will happen.<br /> <br /> That sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T16:18:23-07:00","id":1118745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1118725#post1118725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep.<br /> <br /> If you want Resources, you have to describe it. Describe your business, you land-holdings, your so-on-and-so-forth. That rule comes straight from the book.<br /> <br /> If you want Influence, you have to describe how it works, or how it came about. Why are you so influential in this region?<br /> <br /> If you want Retainers (note that I modified the Retainers merit, so instead of one uberpowerful retainer, you get a larger 'lesser' retinue), you gotta describe where they came from, where you picked them up, how/why you recruited them, why they are loyal to you, so on and so forth.<br /> <br /> If you want Command, you have to describe why the soldiers follow you, and how you keep them supplied.<br /> <br /> If you want Backing..... who backs you, and why? Why are you a member of this organization, who is your superior, how do you feel about each other?<br /> <br /> So on and so forth, for the rest of the Story merits.<br /> <br /> .....perhaps I misspoke. It isn't that I <u>actively dissallow</u> my players from taking Story merits at character creation, it is more that I, well, <i>actually use them in the story</i>. And I prefer to have them gain the Story merits in-play, as a result of their actions, as opposed to just marking things off during character creation.<br /> <br /> For example, let us say Awesome McBadass starts with a Daiklave, looted from his previous incarnation's tomb. So, per the merit, you get your Daiklave...... but, people are going to talk about how <i>someone</i> looted the Anathema MacEvil BigBadEvilGuy's forbidden tomb, braving the dangers within, and escaping with the treasure..... and people are going to ask questions. About how you can carry a blade only the Princes of the Earth can wield, how the hell you survived the place in the first place. Local authority figures are going to be interested, at the very least ...... and depending on how much 'noise&amp;quot; you make looting the joint and surviving the perils, the Wyld Hunt might be called.<br /> <br /> Or..... a Thrifty McMerchant runs a Solar-powered business empire, making beaucoup bucks. Just the Resources merit, right..... but other companies are going to try to make a move on your market, pirates/bandits are going to raid your stuff unless you do something about it, local, or even regional, authority figures are going to try to muscle in on your cash flow, and all the while, resources need to be moved, products need to be produced, and expansion needs to be undertaken.<br /> <br /> All things that, in and of themselves, can, and in my mortal campaigns, often <i>are</i>, stories in and of themselves. In my games, you don't just &amp;quot;get&amp;quot; a merit and mark it down on your character sheet. There are consequences for <i>everything</i>..... not necessarily bad consequences, but things will change, fates will shift, and stuff will happen.<br /> <br /> That sort of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love this actually, and my st does this as well, when we are cooperative enough with him, but I think trying to make backgrounds more than just dots on the page is wonderful, they should add to your character and be tied into how you play out your story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <div align=\"left\">Elemental and dragon line descriptors and capturing device coming soon</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1131843-my-own-take-on-a-craft-rewrite-that-inclu\" target=\"_blank\">Craft Rewrite </a> W/ Points, Slots, and Charms</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1106793-2nd-circle-demon-c-al-siphar-soc-initiation-symbiosis-of-the-burning-heart-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Demon Adversaries and Related Sorcerous Initiation</a></div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1091536-seeking-thoughts-and-suggestions-on-constructing-an-organization-in-game-specifically-a-university\" target=\"_blank\">Executive Leadership</a> Organization Merrit</div> <hr /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1990-norraba","name":"norraba","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1990_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T17:11:53-07:00","id":1118765,"title":"","content":"Don't get me wrong, I approve of using Story Merits to generate stories, but how are the folks learning that a Solar tomb got looted? Was it a Load-Bearing Treasure, where the act of claiming it caused the whole tomb to collapse?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T19:04:21-07:00","id":1118788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1118765#post1118765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't get me wrong, I approve of using Story Merits to generate stories, but how are the folks learning that a Solar tomb got looted? Was it a Load-Bearing Treasure, where the act of claiming it caused the whole tomb to collapse?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there would be good reason to watch Solar Tombs for a variety of reasons. i mean its a SOLAR tomb! These things are dangerous to open and the spoils they contain can be very powerful and valuable, nevermind an escaped and enraged Solar po. Also keeping an eye on Solar tombs can tell you a lot - like if the Solar has been reincarnated and recently looted his tomb. Now you know to mass the Wyld Hunt.<br /> <br /> So I can see Solar Tombs having irregular visits by Sidereal agents and DB shikari to make sure they remain inviolate (and therefore safe from the wrong hands). There would probably be secondary wards and alarms set up around a Solar tomb by these same people to alert them to potential tomb robbers. Even mortal Scavenger Lords could get in on the act with rival factions keeping alarm fetishes set up or spies on station, sabataging each others wards, and whatnot...keeping an eye for when somebody breaks the tomb. When that happens they know loads of potentially very valuable items are going to hit the market, or can be stolen, or you can kill the owners easier than it is to raid a tomb.<br /> <br /> For the record Glen Cook's 'The Silver Spike' is a great story about mortal thieves that breach the defenses warding a immensely powerful artifact and the chaos that follows as the great powers of the world all compete for it. Its a great read and very inspirational about how wrong a successful tomb raid can go for the thieves.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1546,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1546-great-cthulhu","user":"Great Cthulhu","date":". 07-20-2017, 10:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1546-great-cthulhu","name":"Great Cthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1546_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T19:41:45-07:00","id":1118804,"title":"","content":"Huh; interesting.<br /> <br /> \u200bI was all ready to argue against the idea of tombs being recognised and their infiltration being given away, in my usual manner, but...<br /> <br /> Then I thought of Breath of the Wild.<br /> <br /> Dear, beloved Breath of the Wild.<br /> <br /> \u200bA community might forget who the Solars are, and a tomb might become obscured by nature or construction, but if some hint of its presence is kept in a locally repeated poem and any feature of the tomb might change with entry...<br /> <br /> \u200bNot even necessarily something like a light coming on and then changing colour, just the fact that what once looked like a hill now has a big hole in it with some brickwork sticking out...<br /> <br /> That would be enough.<br /> <br /> If the premise is intended to be &quot;the story behind starting with a daiklave entails people telling that story about you&quot;, then all of the necessary conditions are available, and the Storyteller only needs to say that they happened this time.<br /> <br /> Is it unlikely in any given instance that a tomb might have been a feature of interest that some local authorities kept a watch on for any number of reasons?<br /> <br /> Possibly.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhat was I saying earlier about the likelihood of a Solar finding a tomb with a daiklave in it? A few things, really, but they're all generally in the direction of &quot;the likelihood of the backstory is prioritised according to the needs of the actual story&quot;, I think.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo yes, while it's something that I think players necessarily need to be on the same page with, Story Merits at character creation as automatically carrying complications - good idea. My endorsement means nothing, of course, but I just want to express that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T19:43:35-07:00","id":1118806,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1546-great-cthulhu\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1546_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1546\" data-vbnamecard=\"1546\">Great Cthulhu</a>: Yeah, but &quot;DBs/Sidereals are actively watching the tomb to know when it gets successfully looted, and call the Wyld Hunt themselves&quot; is a very different story from the one posited, &quot;people notice the tomb has been looted, local leaders get interested, and from there, the Wyld Hunt may get called.&quot;<br /> <br /> (Also, it still doesn't answer how the observers would <i>know</i> it got looted, unless they are conveniently there to see with their eyes a guy walk in and then back out a day later, glowing, arms heaped with orichalcum. The tombs tend to have very potent defenses, after all, so unless the act of robbing it changes the landscape, or sets free an angry spirit, or whatever, how's the observer able to tell someone made off with the daiklave at the center?)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1118804#post1118804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then I thought of Breath of the Wild.<br /> <br /> Dear, beloved Breath of the Wild\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>When are you going to post the next update for your Let's Play of that game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-20-2017, 10:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T22:02:29-07:00","id":1118833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1118806#post1118806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1546-great-cthulhu\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1546_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1546\" data-vbnamecard=\"1546\">Great Cthulhu</a>: Yeah, but &quot;DBs/Sidereals are actively watching the tomb to know when it gets successfully looted, and call the Wyld Hunt themselves&quot; is a very different story from the one posited, &quot;people notice the tomb has been looted, local leaders get interested, and from there, the Wyld Hunt may get called.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Both stories exist to provoke drama and action in a player character's future. They are equally valid means of doing so. But the point is that information of the tomb robbery can get out, either quickly or slowly, through active surveillance or chance and rumors. Solar tombs and their contents are important enough that people are paying attention to the events and rumors surrounding them. Short of a tomb where all knowledge has been lost tomb robbing them will always be risky and attention getting if done wrong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (Also, it still doesn't answer how the observers would <i>know</i> it got looted, unless they are conveniently there to see with their eyes a guy walk in and then back out a day later, glowing, arms heaped with orichalcum. The tombs tend to have very potent defenses, after all, so unless the act of robbing it changes the landscape, or sets free an angry spirit, or whatever, how's the observer able to tell someone made off with the daiklave at the center?) </div> </div> </div>I provided three examples in my previous post but here goes.<br /> <br /> 1. Patrols by people with the skill and interest to be competent at their jobs. They might not swing by for a while but presumably they will know enough about the tombs to do their job, look for signs of intruders (campsites, footprints, residual magical effects, witnesses), deploy Charms as needed to support their task, etc. Sid agents and DB shikari patrols were both mentioned as having the motivation, the knowledge, and the skill and magical support to be effective at their job. You can easily expand this list if needed.<br /> <br /> 2. Passive magical wards and spells that will alert the appropriate people about potential robbers snooping around the tombs. These don't even have to be part of the original structure. Perhaps they were added late to the surroundings to save on manpower issues or to provide an immediate alarm and response. It need not be Exalted or whatever doing this either. Mortals could place fetishes doing the same thing since many would have an interest in the loot themselves. <br /> <br /> 3. Local spies. Minor gods, local peasants or tribesmen, animals, etc would be in a good position to note any unusual activity and report to their paymasters.<br /> <br /> I'm sure you can come up with other ways besides these three examples.<br /> <br /> And I have to point out that none of these have to immediately show the tomb has been robbed nor do you absolutely need to see Glowing Solar Joe walking out of a busted tomb door shining with orichalcum hardware in order to suspect that a robbery has occurred. Strangers showing unusual interest, a broken tomb door, signs of heavy excavation, residual magics, disturbed spirits, old campsites where nobody goes, unusual artifacts ending up on the local market, and more are all valid evidence of the threat to the tomb or the aftermath of a tomb robbery. And I'll emphasize that Investigation Charms are an excellent way of putting two and two together once you know where to look.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1546-great-cthulhu","name":"Great Cthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1546_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T22:57:31-07:00","id":1118843,"title":"","content":"I'd figured certain signs are just assumed that someone/something has at least attempted to loot the place. Like if it's revealed that the really nice hill near town is actually a burial mound because suddenly there's a door in the side then its a safe bet that someone or something probably went in or came out around the time the door opened. Now obviously this assumption can be correct or incorrect, as a tomb door could have been revealed/opened for any number of reasons, but I certainly wouldn't hold it against a the local village if there were attempts to dissuade people from going in by saying its probably already been picked clean of the easy stuff.<br /> <br /> Actually being part of a team that explored a tomb checking for traps, useful information, or any other things that may be contained therein would be a solid excuse for why a PC might have been in there and even acquired something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T23:08:29-07:00","id":1118846,"title":"","content":"I realize you mentioned Sids and DBs, Cthulhu, but both of those probably feel they have enough on their plates as it is without having to periodically drop everything to verify if a Solar tomb has been successfully penetrated; far likelier is that they'll send some sort of bound spirit to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T00:02:27-07:00","id":1118853,"title":"","content":"Well...sure Sids and DBs are busy beings. But the answer to your original question of how do you notice a tomb robbery is many different ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1546-great-cthulhu","name":"Great Cthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1546_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T00:10:22-07:00","id":1118854,"title":"","content":"I'd prefer no answer to how a PC got their stuff than a boring one. Sometimes elements of backstory just calcify later than others. The only thing that concerns me about players buying artefacts is when they've clearly picked the merits or backgrounds a storyteller can interfere with the least with explanations For how they got them that I can't use as story seeds, it's like the Exalted equivalent of always playing an orphan. I know some people have baggage there but for me it's a big red flag.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12844-bladewind","name":"Bladewind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T03:26:02-07:00","id":1118885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Great Cthulhu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1118853#post1118853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well...sure Sids and DBs are busy beings. But the answer to your original question of how do you notice a tomb robbery is many different ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't disagreeing about the possibility of it - like I said hours ago, the notion of using Story Merits to generate stories is pretty solid.<br /> <br /> Personally I just feel that Artifact has enough <i>other</i> stories it could generate that &quot;the Wyld Hunt hears of it&quot; should barely be worth consideration. Especially with how big a professsion &quot;scavenger lord&quot; is! (Save <i>that</i> for the PC with Influence from living openly as an Anathema!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-21-2017, 06:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T07:47:56-07:00","id":1118958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1118725#post1118725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep.<br /> <br /> If you want Resources, you have to describe it. Describe your business, you land-holdings, your so-on-and-so-forth. That rule comes straight from the book.<br /> <br /> If you want Influence, you have to describe how it works, or how it came about. Why are you so influential in this region?<br /> <br /> If you want Retainers (note that I modified the Retainers merit, so instead of one uberpowerful retainer, you get a larger 'lesser' retinue), you gotta describe where they came from, where you picked them up, how/why you recruited them, why they are loyal to you, so on and so forth.<br /> <br /> If you want Command, you have to describe why the soldiers follow you, and how you keep them supplied.<br /> <br /> If you want Backing..... who backs you, and why? Why are you a member of this organization, who is your superior, how do you feel about each other?<br /> <br /> So on and so forth, for the rest of the Story merits.<br /> <br /> .....perhaps I misspoke. It isn't that I <u>actively dissallow</u> my players from taking Story merits at character creation, it is more that I, well, <i>actually use them in the story</i>. And I prefer to have them gain the Story merits in-play, as a result of their actions, as opposed to just marking things off during character creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that seems fairly normal. You can't really run half the backgrounds without knowing the details, honestly.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T15:50:47-07:00","id":1119096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1118658#post1118658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Emphases mine. It looks to me, and maybe I'm misinterpreting, that in your game at your table I cannot have a daiklave I found in my Solar tomb.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I would let you have one, though I could see why you would assume you couldn't. I mean, there is a pretty silly bit of misinformation that all artifact weapons have a minimum rating of 3 floating about, but I've found it's never a good idea to constrain yourself that much. For preference I'd work with you on the background itself to make it was something more fitting to the game and to eliminate the tomb thing entirely, but if that's really what you want to roll with I'd let you.<br /> <br /> Since I as per usual already have the fiery sticks and farm implements crowd after me, I would also add that I would strongly suggest taking <i>Summoning the Loyal Steel</i> or something, because once gameplay starts I don't consider your character sheet sacrosanct. You drop yer grand killstick down a bottomless pit and don't have any way to retrieve it, then it's gone, and you don't automatically trip over a new one or a talent of jade to reimburse you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (Without bribery, which is a whole different can of worms.) </div> </div> </div>It's a can of worms with the rather crowded label of &quot;Bribing the GM with Dice and Food Has Been a Gaming Culture Joke Since at Least 1979 That I Am Aware of But Which I Apparently Now Need To Be Extremely Unsubtle and Blatant About Because I Think People Are Purposefully Being Disingenuous About it In Order to Take Cheap Shots At Me in This Thread.&quot; <br /> <br /> They have very poor brand recognition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1118713#post1118713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You absolute evil monster</div> </div> </div> </div>Please, stop flattering me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1118693#post1118693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A: 3d6 averages 10.5. In any of the last three editions having an 11 in your main stat is the next best thing to worthless. In 3 and 4 it makes you even more dependent on the magic item christmas tree to perform your party role since monster CR was balanced around the heroic array AND the christmas tree. In 5 you are just bad at your job which brings things back to everyone already having experience with roleplaying puny mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>If your sole metric for determining effectivness is raw stats, than I have some kobolds that I think you should meet.<br /> <br /> I've seen plenty of 18/00 Strength, 18 Con fighters get their shit absolutely wrecked by &quot;weaker&quot; opponents because those opponents were faster, smarter, more cunning.<br /> <br /> It ain't just what you got, it's how you use it too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> C: Why should someone have to play a thief who always wanted to be a warrior? Yes, that is a character some people want to play. But if you signed up to play Conan it is unsatisfying because you are being told you aren't allowed to play what you want. </div> </div> </div>Maybe have some flexibility in your character concept? If you go into a game willing to accept Conan and just Conan otherwise you do the gaming Internet tough guy &quot;No gaming is better than bad gaming, my concept 100% or I walk&quot; stuff, that's on you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So it is less than worthless and the player appears to have recognized that. </div> </div> </div>No, it's an implement of unfettered chaos magic and acts as one. Just turns out that our Chaotic Neutral warlock may not have been as big a fan of chaos as he thought; this is sorta backed up because he decided to join the Fated instead of the Xaosetects.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Between the possible good/bad/neither results I am going to bet the number that are good are a minority. </div> </div> </div>Ah, this is my favorite bit of your post, the snide insinuation that I purposefully stacked the deck against my player, because...I don't know, laughs?<br /> <br /> I can tell you that the effect able is actually fairly balanced between potentially targeting the user, the target or the environment. As for good/bad...well, that's harder to judge. Is convincing the target that he's a balloon and will pop if punctured a good thing? Is changing the street cobbles to dirt a bad thing? There are several NPCs who will now burst into butterflies when they die, whenever or however that happens; neutral? You tell me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So to use it in any important situation is a waste of an action at best </div> </div> </div>If they want something safe and predictable, they're in the position to walk down to the Bazaar and start pricing a <i>wand of fireballs</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Add to the fact that you made it annoying and all you have done is put words on his inventory list that everyone is going to ignore or given them a mcguffin whose properties almost don't matter to be bartered or blown up later </div> </div> </div>All sentient magical items are obnoxious. Tru fax. And Willie Wizwunkler the Wonspectuaclar Wizardly W-Extrodinarie Wand of Wonderousness and Wantoness <i>really</i> likes causing chaos and making things go boom.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How has this improved anyone's play experience? </div> </div> </div>He's really fun to roleplay, the party enjoys talking with him, he shouts &quot;Behold!&quot; a lot and likes to claim credit for everything magical that happens around him, and considers everything that happens when the party uses him to the pinnacle of magical and spellcasting genius, even if the wand just shoots out bubbles or something. I'm half-hoping that, once the party catches up with the current villains, they use Willie on them a lot; the party would probably see it as justice for all the grief they've been getting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T17:07:19-07:00","id":1119115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1119096#post1119096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a can of worms with the rather crowded label of &quot;Bribing the GM with Dice and Food Has Been a Gaming Culture Joke Since at Least 1979 That I Am Aware of But Which I Apparently Now Need To Be Extremely Unsubtle and Blatant About Because I Think People Are Purposefully Being Disingenuous About it In Order to Take Cheap Shots At Me in This Thread.&quot;<br /> <br /> They have very poor brand recognition.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bSpeaking in what I hope are sincere and conciliatory tones:<br /> <br /> \u200bI think that not everybody here is really part of that wider culture.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> update </div> </div> </div>Ehh, later. Technical and creative issues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T04:10:06-07:00","id":1119223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1118693#post1118693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you are charging people real money for words on paper when they already spent real money to buy the books, took time to make their characters, and blocked out several hours when they could be doing something else? Because they weren't good enough to pass your creative writing test to your arbitrary standards? Because the fact that they are at the table <i>at all</i> doesn't already show an immense commitment?</div> </div> </div> </div>I know it can be difficult to tell when Coik is joking sometimes but you're essentially accusing him of extorting his players which is a bit beyond the pale. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T21:00:23-07:00","id":1119395,"title":"","content":"My go-to for my signature character is taking Summoning the Loyal Steel as a starting charm and writing its appearance into the exaltation back-story. So at first, this Fair Folk thinks it has this mortal cornered, then... boom! Dawn Caste exaltation with an orichalcum grand daiklave literally in hand.<br /> <br /> ('But when one of the exalted dies, anything stored Elsewhere drops to the ground next to their corpse!' --yeah, don't care.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/994-heroicantagonist","name":"heroicantagonist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar994_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T21:22:18-07:00","id":1119398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heroicantagonist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1119395#post1119395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">('But when one of the exalted dies, anything stored Elsewhere drops to the ground next to their corpse!' --yeah, don't care.)</div> </div> </div> </div>That's if it's stored Elsewhere. Has a very different result then if the Solar has a tendency to misplace things and it resulted in the charm storing things, elsewhere. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T00:14:24-07:00","id":1119429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heroicantagonist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1119395#post1119395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">('But when one of the exalted dies, anything stored Elsewhere drops to the ground next to their corpse!' --yeah, don't care.)</div> </div> </div> </div>That was a houserule made for Keychain of Creation so the story would work; in 1e and 2e, unless it was cached in a Cache Egg, the storing Exalt's death caused it to effectively <b>be lost forever</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T00:19:59-07:00","id":1119430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1119429#post1119429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was a houserule made for Keychain of Creation so the story would work; in 1e and 2e, unless it was cached in a Cache Egg, the storing Exalt's death caused it to effectively <b>be lost forever</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would agree with the comic depicting the crafter entering &quot;elsewhere&quot; and being surrounded by hundreds of lost artifacts, also sadly in effect being lost himself. <br /> <br /> Can't remember the book for reference right now, I will find it in the morning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <div align=\"left\">Elemental and dragon line descriptors and capturing device coming soon</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1131843-my-own-take-on-a-craft-rewrite-that-inclu\" target=\"_blank\">Craft Rewrite </a> W/ Points, Slots, and Charms</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1106793-2nd-circle-demon-c-al-siphar-soc-initiation-symbiosis-of-the-burning-heart-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Demon Adversaries and Related Sorcerous Initiation</a></div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1091536-seeking-thoughts-and-suggestions-on-constructing-an-organization-in-game-specifically-a-university\" target=\"_blank\">Executive Leadership</a> Organization Merrit</div> <hr /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1990-norraba","name":"norraba","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1990_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T00:45:51-07:00","id":1119431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>norraba</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1119430#post1119430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would agree with the comic depicting the crafter entering &quot;elsewhere&quot; and being surrounded by hundreds of lost artifacts, also sadly in effect being lost himself.<br /> <br /> Can't remember the book for reference right now, I will find it in the morning.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I THINK it was Oadenol's Codex.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T00:53:18-07:00","id":1119432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1119429#post1119429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was a houserule made for Keychain of Creation so the story would work; in 1e and 2e, unless it was cached in a Cache Egg, the storing Exalt's death caused it to effectively <b>be lost forever</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Ex2 (and still so in Ex3), objects stored Elsewhere explicitly reappeared beside the Solar whenever the Summoning the Loyal (Whatsit) charms' mote commitment ended.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt is true that Cache Eggs remain banished to Elsewhere when their owners die (the motes used to banish them are not committed). However, these can <i>sometimes </i>be recalled by future incarnations (conditions apply).<br /> <br /> Additionally an attempt to banish a second Cache Egg that shatters the first, <i>exiling </i>that egg and its contents from the world. (<i>BoS I: Wonders of the Lost Age</i> pg 58.) <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>norraba</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1119430#post1119430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would agree with the comic depicting the crafter entering &quot;elsewhere&quot; and being surrounded by hundreds of lost artifacts, also sadly in effect being lost himself.<br /> <br /> Can't remember the book for reference right now, I will find it in the morning.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the cartoon is on the <b>Book of Sorcery III: Oadenol's Codex</b>'s page 8, and there is no mention of the artefacts being lost<i> per se</i>. The Twilight invented an Elsewhere Transporter to access artefacts that were &quot;<i>stored safely</i>&quot; and discovered things in Elsewhere couldn't move, including himself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 07-23-2017, 04:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T00:57:00-07:00","id":1119433,"title":"","content":"I never liked that comic as it reinforced the idea of Elsewhere as a dimension where all the things sent there float in a void.<br /> <br /> I much prefer the idea that &quot;Elsewhere&quot; is simply the state of existing without external location. It's Nirupadhika.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T08:53:23-07:00","id":1119530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts#post1116730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I asked about whether Arms of the Chosen will touch on this in the developer thread, but I'm curious what people's experience at their own table has been. It's easy enough to justify the personal arsenal of starting Dynast PCs, or Deathknights, or Sidereals. Even the Lunars, though they have less infrastructure than those, have the Silver Pact which might specifically pass on something that belonged to the PC's previous incarnation, or receive a gift from a mentor, etc.<br /> <br /> What about Solars though? Plenty of character concepts call for starting the game with your signature daiklaive, or powerbow, etc. But how do you narratively explain how a brand new Solar came into the possession of such an artifact? Does everyone just go with &quot;visions led you to the tomb of your First Age incarnation&quot;, or have you found more diverse answers to the question?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a number of Solars prebuilt, only some of which start with artifacts.<br /> <br /> The Zenith rockstar had his made for him in Hell after performing there. And yes, he has positive inimacies to the demon who made them.<br /> <br /> The Night was guided to a past live safe house when she was on the run during her exaltation, and the safehouse had a chainshirt.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T08:02:13-07:00","id":1120354,"title":"","content":"An Eclipse Caste Solar I created received her artifacts from a forest spirit she rescued from an Abyssal's attempt to corrupt. In a previous incarnation, the spirit offered her sanctuary from the Dragon-Blooded that were hunting her during the Usurpation... but when a Sidereal threatened to destroy the spirit, her previous incarnation chose to sacrifice herself to protect him... gifting him with the oricalcum necklace (collar of dawn's cleansing light) she wore as a memento of their time together (and the promise that she would return one day). The day (actually night) she exalted and saved the spirit in her current incarnation was the fulfilment of that promise... and in the morning, the spirit gifted her with the necklace and an additional gift (for saving his life once again)... a gown of Silken Armor (made in memory of her previous incarnation).<br /> <br /> \u200bThere are many ways that even starting Solars can receive artifacts... some more common than others. As long as there is a good (and more or less plausible) backstory to how it was acquired... I have no problem letting players start with them (I'll even make suggestions to help spur their imaginations to come up with such stories). By the same token, I have run a few games where the players were specifically told they couldn't start the game with various backgrounds (including Artifacts) because of 1) how the game was going to start and 2) because they would eventually raid the tombs of their previous incarnations and obtain some artifacts to help them on their adventures. The players actually had a fair bit of fun because they could focus on other aspects of their characters without sacrificing something they wanted for something they sometimes believed they needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T13:12:31-07:00","id":1120460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1119433#post1119433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never liked that comic as it reinforced the idea of Elsewhere as a dimension where all the things sent there float in a void.<br /> <br /> I much prefer the idea that &quot;Elsewhere&quot; is simply the state of existing without external location. It's Nirupadhika.</div> </div> </div> </div>Compass of Celestial Directions: Elsewhere.<br /> <br /> (Also, <i>Compass of Celestial Directions: The Endless Darkness Outside Existence</i>, for those people hit by that one ED charm.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T03:55:29-07:00","id":1120726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1119433#post1119433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never liked that comic as it reinforced the idea of Elsewhere as a dimension where all the things sent there float in a void.<br /> <br /> I much prefer the idea that &amp;quot;Elsewhere&amp;quot; is simply the state of existing without external location. It's Nirupadhika.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno. If you went there, it's probably be a void with stuff floating in it.<br /> <br /> Or you'd just die in darkness. Probably that. Where does the light in the void come from anyways?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T05:07:24-07:00","id":1120751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Childofthesun1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1120726#post1120726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dunno. If you went there, it's probably be a void with stuff floating in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, that requires spatial relationships between the different objects that are Elsewhere. And if my interpretation is correct, they'd lack any such relationship.<br /> <br /> If someone somehow got sent Elsewhere, I'd just have them experience a vision trip from stuff in their own head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T07:48:01-07:00","id":1120792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1120751#post1120751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nah, that requires spatial relationships between the different objects that are Elsewhere. And if my interpretation is correct, they'd lack any such relationship.<br /> <br /> If someone somehow got sent Elsewhere, I'd just have them experience a vision trip from stuff in their own head.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, my brain doesn't get the abstract stuff in Exalted. What does a dimension without spatial relation even look like? I just shutdown and ignore whatever that is.<br /> <br /> Like higher dimensions in fiction, like a fifth dimension or something. What even is that? If, by my very nature, I can't understand that, the logic part of my brain just says &quot;that's dumb&quot; and shuts down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T07:58:22-07:00","id":1120799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Childofthesun1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1120792#post1120792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, my brain doesn't get the abstract stuff in Exalted. What does a dimension without spatial relation even look like? I just shutdown and ignore whatever that is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't even think of Elsewhere as a dimension. It's just the state of not having a location.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T07:58:38-07:00","id":1120800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Childofthesun1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1120792#post1120792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does a dimension without spatial relation even look like?</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't look like anything, because there's no conduit for information between your brain and anything else.<br /> <br /> \u200b(Strictly speaking, nothing actually looks like anything; our perceptions are a result of our brains processing input based on electromagnetic interactions)<br /> <br /> \u200bPoint is, a person placed elsewhere would probably exist in a state of total sensory deprivation, something that would very quickly destroy their cognitive processes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T08:25:02-07:00","id":1120809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1120800#post1120800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It doesn't look like anything, because there's no conduit for information between your brain and anything else.<br /> <br /> \u200b(Strictly speaking, nothing actually looks like anything; our perceptions are a result of our brains processing input based on electromagnetic interactions)<br /> <br /> \u200bPoint is, a person placed elsewhere would probably exist in a state of total sensory deprivation, something that would very quickly destroy their cognitive processes.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it's a series of seperate pocket dimensions? The particles the object is made of clearly still have location data relative to each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T08:25:49-07:00","id":1120810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1120799#post1120799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't even think of Elsewhere as a dimension. It's just the state of not having a location.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does something not have a location? What does that even mean?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T08:28:44-07:00","id":1120813,"title":"","content":"Any living thing that goes into elsewhere unless frozen would probably die. There is nothing to respire and no separation between the various substances the body goes to such lengths not to mix. <br /> Also, there may be no arrow of time since there may be no means to construct a clock.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T08:32:25-07:00","id":1120817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1120813#post1120813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any living thing that goes into elsewhere unless frozen would probably die. There is nothing to respire and no separation between the various substances the body goes to such lengths not to mix. <br /> Also, there may be no arrow of time since there may be no means to construct a clock.</div> </div> </div> </div>So all your individual molecules occupy the same space, but it's probably okay because there's no time for you to die because there IS NO TIME and because you'll just be reconstructed when you exit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T08:36:21-07:00","id":1120821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Childofthesun1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1120809#post1120809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So it's a series of seperate pocket dimensions? The particles the object is made of clearly still have location data relative to each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exalted is not science fiction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T08:41:38-07:00","id":1120826,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Childofthesun1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1120809#post1120809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it's a series of separate pocket dimensions? The particles the object is made of clearly still have location data relative to each other.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#222222\">The particles, if those exist in the first place, only appear to have location data relative to each other because of one comic. And there are pockets like Autochthonia that do not appear to interact with anything else that is elsewhere. However, his primordial mythos may be altering the usual rules.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\">You can also apparently fold space into elsewhere like a dimension (like the 4th rather than pocket which aren't really dimensions) to make them bigger on the inside or create shorter paths from A to B.</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Childofthesun1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1120810#post1120810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does something not have a location? What does that even mean?</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#222222\">Where is justice? Justice is a thing, there is a noun for it and everything. Where is it? Replace with a similar abstract noun if needed.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Childofthesun1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1120817#post1120817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\">So all your individual molecules occupy the same space, but it's probably okay because there's no time for you to die because there IS NO TIME and because you'll just be reconstructed when you exit?</span></div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\">Molecules may not exist in Exalted, at least in 2E everything was </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:21px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">essence</span></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">. And there would have to be a space for them to occupy in the first place. Crushed down into a black hole is still </span></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">a space</span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"> which elsewhere may not have.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T08:52:33-07:00","id":1120834,"title":"","content":"So If I'm gathering this right, transporting objects to elsewhere is essentially viewed by the community as being similar to teleporting something in Star Trek, but then storing what you've teleported as data in the data buffer. It still exists but not really?<br /> <br /> This is a bit confusing considering I got into exalted late into 2nd edition and most of the books were out already, so the comic from odenols, plus the fact that the entire demon realm and autochthon existed in elsewhere never made me think of it this way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <div align=\"left\">Elemental and dragon line descriptors and capturing device coming soon</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1131843-my-own-take-on-a-craft-rewrite-that-inclu\" target=\"_blank\">Craft Rewrite </a> W/ Points, Slots, and Charms</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1106793-2nd-circle-demon-c-al-siphar-soc-initiation-symbiosis-of-the-burning-heart-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Demon Adversaries and Related Sorcerous Initiation</a></div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1091536-seeking-thoughts-and-suggestions-on-constructing-an-organization-in-game-specifically-a-university\" target=\"_blank\">Executive Leadership</a> Organization Merrit</div> <hr /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1990-norraba","name":"norraba","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1990_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T08:59:58-07:00","id":1120837,"title":"","content":"Elsewhere is the kind of thing that is intended to function solely off of the most superficial observations of it.<br /> <br /> \u200bYou commit some motes, and your weapon vanishes until you call it back to yourself. That does not meaningfully function off of something independent of the Charm used to do it, or a phenomenon that can be independently manipulated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T09:01:47-07:00","id":1120839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1120826#post1120826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\">The particles, if those exist in the first place, only appear to have location data relative to each other because of one comic. And there are pockets like Autochthonia that do not appear to interact with anything else that is elsewhere. However, his primordial mythos may be altering the usual rules.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\">You can also apparently fold space into elsewhere like a dimension (like the 4th rather than pocket which aren't really dimensions) to make them bigger on the inside or create shorter paths from A to B.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\">Where is justice? Justice is a thing, there is a noun for it and everything. Where is it? Replace with a similar abstract noun if needed.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\">Molecules may not exist in Exalted, at least in 2E everything was </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:21px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">essence</span></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">. And there would have to be a space for them to occupy in the first place. Crushed down into a black hole is still </span></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">a space</span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"> which elsewhere may not have.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Justice is not a physical variable you can interact with. It's an idea or emotion. Location is a very tangible thing I interact with constantly. I understand &quot;other dimensions&quot; or &quot;parallel worlds&quot; being a thing where you can store stuff, but &quot;it has no location&quot; conceptually makes no sense, like an object with no mass. Just...how?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T09:02:22-07:00","id":1120840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1120821#post1120821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exalted is not science fiction.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was extraordinarily unhelpful, thanks. :/","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T09:22:25-07:00","id":1120851,"title":"","content":"My good will is rapidly diminishing, but for the moment...<br /> <br /> \u200bExalted, as I would say with most things involving magic, is not concerned with breaking down and analysing the properties of what it represents. Mystical things such as this are elemental and generally just limited to what is directly observed and intuited. That's why you can make a spell that ends at a period such as &quot;sunset&quot;, despite that being an arbitrary and ambiguous time period. Or how somebody can conjure up a flame that doesn't have anything like a fuel source; logically, the dynamics of how it works would have to be extremely different from actual flames, but that doesn't matter so long as it resembles what people recognise a flame to look like.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe idea of sending a personal possession to some basically defined non-space is not something with any intention of being reconciled with physics, or broken down in any way, anymore than Lunar shapeshifting has any concern with thermodynamics. It simply happens, because it's artistic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T10:05:58-07:00","id":1120875,"title":"","content":"Elsewhere is hammerspace. That's it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T10:12:46-07:00","id":1120878,"title":"","content":"A thing you place Elsewhere is axiomatically 1) available for you to retrieve within the specifications of the talent that allowed you to put it there, 2) inaccessible to anyone other than yourself [barring, say, a hypothetical charm that makes you axiomatically such a master thief you can steal things that are Elsewhere], and 3) not where you are.<br /> <br /> There is no greater explanation, no need for some Elsewhere Dimension that can be plotted and charted and accessed and ventured into. The aforementioned things tell you everything you need to know.<br /> &quot;Can I access my sword?&quot; It is Elsewhere, so yes, as per Summoning the Loyal Steel, it is in your hand at a moment's notice.<br /> &quot;Can he steal my sword?&quot; It is Elsewhere, so no, unless he has some explicitly defined ability to steal things that are Elsewhere, he cannot steal it.<br /> &quot;If someone magically and perfectly destroys all Swords where I am, is my sword okay?&quot; It is Elsewhere, so yes, it is unharmed.<br /> <br /> You can make up an explanation for Elsewhere Pseudoparticle Gammeta Radiation, but that's going to be entirely your headcanon; the current edition seems to not want to overexplain things, preferring straightforward explanations as above, so it's highly unlikely that we'll even get a comic like that one [stupid] WaddyCodex one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","user":"Meianno Yuurei","date":". 07-26-2017, 01:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T10:52:56-07:00","id":1120902,"title":"","content":"So, would anybody ever do a story in which they received their Artifact by it inexplicably appearing before them in some mystical display in a time of need, leaving some kind of hanging mystery that might never be addressed or resolved behind it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T11:14:48-07:00","id":1120912,"title":"","content":"I'd let my players do it, because I'm sure I could come up with some interesting plot for it (as long as it was just one or two artefacts, not 4 or 5) but if I wanted to do it I'd ask the ST how they felt about it, because I could see that it might seem like you're too lazy to come up with your own backstory and want the ST to do it for you.<br /> I have a friend who was ST of a Vampire Larp, and he got quite annoyed with all the characters with Amnesia and Dark Secret, because it seemed like they just wanted him to come up with a backstory for them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T11:18:36-07:00","id":1120913,"title":"","content":"So this all started when we were discussing what Elsewhere looks like. I took issue with the use of &quot;Has no location&quot; because it makes me feel the same way as hearing &quot;what's the sound of one hand clapping&quot;: confused and frustrated.<br /> <br /> My answer to the question is &quot;pocket dimension&quot; with an implicit understanding that that's a thing from pop culture. It sounds like everyone else's answer is &quot;this is a dumb question&quot; or &quot;the answer doesn't matter.&quot; Those are valid answers!<br /> <br /> &quot;Has no location&quot; is still a frustrating answer though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T11:39:59-07:00","id":1120927,"title":"","content":"I like to imagine the Solar keeps his daiklaive inside his soul, and then pulls it out of his soul when it's time for stabbing.<br /> But really, it doesn't matter that much, it's just a way to be able to have a ridiculous giant sword in a fight and not have to worry about where to keep it when you are partying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T12:20:40-07:00","id":1120946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1120912#post1120912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wanted to do it I'd ask the ST how they felt about it, because I could see that it might seem like you're too lazy to come up with your own backstory and want the ST to do it for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWell, like I said, I wouldn't think it strictly needs to be resolved.<br /> <br /> \u200bIf it was me, I would explain that I'm perfectly amenable to the idea of it being something that plays into Creation occasionally being home to either the inexplicably mystical or ill-fated machinations.<br /> <br /> \u200bLike the idea of some god or demon who thought getting the sword out there like that would be a good way to draw somebody's attention in a manner engendering a bit of awe, and then becomes frustrated when it turns out that the Solar isn't especially interested and the spirit can't really approach them personally, and so they never meet.<br /> <br /> \u200bMy worldview informs my fondness for the idea of stories in which things inexplicable things happen because one never finds or cares to seek the context, and the idea of lives and events being shaped by human activities and interactions that never get told to anybody.<br /> <br /> \u200bLike how the HBO Rome series depicts the inciting event of Caesar's civil war being when one of Marc Antony's supporters is attacked by somebody whose brother he killed, and everybody else assumes that the attacker was going for Antony and was one of Pompey's supporters, or a certain Samurai Jack episode*.<br /> <br /> \u200bEvery now and then, while somewhere far from civilization, Solars should get attacked by a group of ninjas; after they're killed, the Solars realise that they have no idea who sent the attackers or why, and even if they care to redirect themselves significantly to investigate, odds are that there would be insufficient leads anyway.<br /> <br /> \u200b* <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The one where the whole episode follows a robot that gets coerced by Aku into going after Jack by taking its dog, who then destroys it in an instant, and nobody ever knows the poor robot's story.</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T12:32:56-07:00","id":1120957,"title":"","content":"My Dawn player baked his Artifact into his backstory, he Exalted because he got the Daiklaive. It was the classic &quot;sword in the stone&quot; scenario, except rather than there being no one worthy to pull it, no one could get close cause it shot lightning bolts at any who approached. One day this wandering swordsman walks up, thinks &quot;I'll give it a try&quot; and approaches the shine holding the sword. The bolt shot out, and in a flash of golden light, he batted it aside with his sword. Then another one came, and another one. Those got the same treatment, parried away by the newly minted Dawn Caste, and the Daiklaive had found a new owner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13696-knurlurzhad","name":"Knurlurzhad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13696_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T14:24:36-07:00","id":1121021,"title":"","content":"Personally, I see Elsewhere as a sort of &quot;anti-wyld&quot;, it's polar opposite. The Wyld is chaos, and it only have distance if someone wills it. Elsewhere is void of chaos, and only has form or distance if something is placed there from the outside. There is no time there, so things age. Mortals and most deities would not survive being put in Elsewhere, at least not without being put inside something protecting then (like the body of Malfeas). In my game, Yu-shan is also located in Elsewhere. Just because Malfeas and Yu-shan has time don't mean the protective bubble has to have time inside it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1120946#post1120946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bMy worldview informs my fondness for the idea of stories in which things inexplicable things happen because one never finds or cares to seek the context, and the idea of lives and events being shaped by human activities and interactions that never get told to anybody.<br /> <br /> \u200bLike how the HBO Rome series depicts the inciting event of Caesar's civil war being when one of Marc Antony's supporters is attacked by somebody whose brother he killed, and everybody else assumes that the attacker was going for Antony and was one of Pompey's supporters, or a certain Samurai Jack episode*.</div> </div> </div> </div>Different tastes. While some don't mind if it is inexplicable to the ST, some players (and some STs) want there to be an explanation, even if it never reaches the player characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T14:34:54-07:00","id":1121024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1121021#post1121021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I see Elsewhere as a sort of &amp;quot;anti-wyld&amp;quot;, it's polar opposite. The Wyld is chaos, and it only have distance if someone wills it. Elsewhere is void of chaos, and only has form or distance if something is placed there from the outside. There is no time there, so things age. Mortals and most deities would not survive being put in Elsewhere, at least not without being put inside something protecting then (like the body of Malfeas). In my game, Yu-shan is also located in Elsewhere. Just because Malfeas and Yu-shan has time don't mean the protective bubble has to have time inside it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Different tastes. While some don't mind if it is inexplicable to the ST, some players (and some STs) want there to be an explanation, even if it never reaches the player characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>So how does Elsewhere connect to Creation? Is it directional, like go far enough up and you'll end up in Elsewhere? There's a general sense that Underworld=down, Wyld=around, and Yu-Shan and Malfeas are ???","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T15:23:28-07:00","id":1121050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1120902#post1120902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, would anybody ever do a story in which they received their Artifact by it inexplicably appearing before them in some mystical display in a time of need, leaving some kind of hanging mystery that might never be addressed or resolved behind it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I discussed doing just that kind of thing with a player when we were brainstorming his last character : having a daiklaive fall from the sky like a meteor to allow him to change the tide of battles. We talked about potential explanations for it, with the idea of maybe exploring them in-play.<br /> <br /> In the end, his character concept changed, so we never did that, but I still like the idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ultimate Jade-Screened Exalted Scholar, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304239-my-next-campaign-tdhr-peach\" target=\"_blank\">THDR : Future Dragon-Blooded campaign</a>, and other links.<br /> If you like Ex3, you can support <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/holdenshearer\" target=\"_blank\">Holden</a> on Patreon!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","name":"LeTipex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T15:50:33-07:00","id":1121060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Childofthesun1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1121024#post1121024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So how does Elsewhere connect to Creation? Is it directional, like go far enough up and you'll end up in Elsewhere? There's a general sense that Underworld=down, Wyld=around, and Yu-Shan and Malfeas are ???</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, Elsewhere is all around Creation. The Underworld isn't in my mind downwards, but overlapping (as a parallel dimension of sort).<br /> <br /> But unlike the Underworld, I don't see Elsewhere overlapping. The lack of distance in Elsewhere is what makes it possible to reach something put there from wherever, and why Elsewhere can fit something as large as Malfeas without problem. If you're familiar with low level programming, the access to something in Elsewhere has more in common with memory pointers than a three (or two) dimensional coordination system. In that comparison, Elsewhere would be an enormous (or infinite) memory bank.<br /> <br /> This is why it is shorter to use two Yu-shan gates, than go the same distance through Creation. Both Creation and Yu-shan follows the logic of a Cartesian coordination system, but Elsewhere do not. For example, I see no reason for the placements of the gates in Yu-shan, other than it feels more &quot;logical&quot; to have a gate in the eastern part of Yu-shan connected to an eastern part of Creation. They could as well have been placed at random (which is also why getting in and out of Malfeas tend to be a bit ... wonky).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T16:29:03-07:00","id":1121079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Childofthesun1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1120839#post1120839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Justice is not a physical variable you can interact with. It's an idea or emotion. Location is a very tangible thing I interact with constantly. I understand &quot;other dimensions&quot; or &quot;parallel worlds&quot; being a thing where you can store stuff, but &quot;it has no location&quot; conceptually makes no sense, like an object with no mass. Just...how?</div> </div> </div> </div>If it makes sense is beside the point. It is a fact of the setting (at least in 2E) that things with such properties as make no sense are real.<br /> <br /> Take the Shinma. They are really an exercise in set theory, but they existed in both the prior editions. Casually first of the Shinma is Nirguna. She, despite having a name and a gender and being discussed, does not exist. Her non-existence is necessary for the existence of everything else, because by not existing she defines what it means to exist. <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">http://rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/index.php/Shinma</span></span></span></span> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T16:43:59-07:00","id":1121086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1121021#post1121021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I see Elsewhere as a sort of &quot;anti-wyld&quot;, it's polar opposite. The Wyld is chaos, and it only have distance if someone wills it. Elsewhere is void of chaos, and only has form or distance if something is placed there from the outside. There is no time there, so things age. Mortals and most deities would not survive being put in Elsewhere, at least not without being put inside something protecting then (like the body of Malfeas). In my game, Yu-shan is also located in Elsewhere. Just because Malfeas and Yu-shan has time don't mean the protective bubble has to have time inside it.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1121060#post1121060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, Elsewhere is all around Creation. The Underworld isn't in my mind downwards, but overlapping (as a parallel dimension of sort).<br /> <br /> But unlike the Underworld, I don't see Elsewhere overlapping. The lack of distance in Elsewhere is what makes it possible to reach something put there from wherever, and why Elsewhere can fit something as large as Malfeas without problem. If you're familiar with low level programming, the access to something in Elsewhere has more in common with memory pointers than a three (or two) dimensional coordination system. In that comparison, Elsewhere would be an enormous (or infinite) memory bank.<br /> <br /> This is why it is shorter to use two Yu-shan gates, than go the same distance through Creation. Both Creation and Yu-shan follows the logic of a Cartesian coordination system, but Elsewhere do not. For example, I see no reason for the placements of the gates in Yu-shan, other than it feels more &quot;logical&quot; to have a gate in the eastern part of Yu-shan connected to an eastern part of Creation. They could as well have been placed at random (which is also why getting in and out of Malfeas tend to be a bit ... wonky).</div> </div> </div> </div>i really like this, i think it will form the basis for my concept of elsewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <div align=\"left\">Elemental and dragon line descriptors and capturing device coming soon</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1131843-my-own-take-on-a-craft-rewrite-that-inclu\" target=\"_blank\">Craft Rewrite </a> W/ Points, Slots, and Charms</div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1106793-2nd-circle-demon-c-al-siphar-soc-initiation-symbiosis-of-the-burning-heart-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Demon Adversaries and Related Sorcerous Initiation</a></div> <div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1091536-seeking-thoughts-and-suggestions-on-constructing-an-organization-in-game-specifically-a-university\" target=\"_blank\">Executive Leadership</a> Organization Merrit</div> <hr /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1990-norraba","name":"norraba","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1990_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T18:26:48-07:00","id":1121125,"title":"","content":"Still far too much elaboration on a concept that is essentially simple.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlthough I do think there's something funny in the idea of seeking an actual direction in which to pursue Elsewhere, since anything that you can actually reach is, by definition, not Elsewhere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LeTipex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1121050#post1121050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I discussed doing just that kind of thing with a player when we were brainstorming his last character : having a daiklaive fall from the sky like a meteor to allow him to change the tide of battles. We talked about potential explanations for it, with the idea of maybe exploring them in-play.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's similar to an idea I proposed in a previous thread on this subject, with the somewhat tongue-in-cheek notion that it could have been sent flying in a particularly dramatic disarm move incurred by an Exalt a few hundred miles away.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T19:39:43-07:00","id":1121156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1121079#post1121079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it makes sense is beside the point. It is a fact of the setting (at least in 2E) that things with such properties as make no sense are real.<br /> <br /> Take the Shinma. They are really an exercise in set theory, but they existed in both the prior editions. Casually first of the Shinma is Nirguna. She, despite having a name and a gender and being discussed, does not exist. Her non-existence is necessary for the existence of everything else, because by not existing she defines what it means to exist. <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">http://rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/index.php/Shinma</span></span></span></span> <br /> </div> </div> </div> </div>And esoteric bullshit infuriates me because it seems like a futile exercise in illogic committed by stoners. &quot;Like, what if nothing was a thing. And what if everything only existed because nothing, like, makes everything exist, maaan?&quot; That makes no sense. I'm cool with the Wyld vomiting forth twisted, howling monstrosities and the landscape shifting in nightmarish and hostile ways, that's fine. &quot;Up is down&quot; is comprehensible. &quot;Up is glurple&quot; is incomprehensible and is neither entertaining for me to read nor feasible to play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T19:51:17-07:00","id":1121157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Childofthesun1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1120809#post1120809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So it's a series of seperate pocket dimensions? The particles the object is made of clearly still have location data relative to each other.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Separate dimension pockets is closer to what I mean than a single big space where Yu Shan in an Adamant-bubble and Autochthon float around with people's stuff. Way more scifi terminology than I'd use for Exalted, but if dimensions help people conceptualize how two realms can have no spatial relationship to each other - and then apply that same principle on an object scale, then sure that analogy works fine.<br /> <br /> Creation doesn't have particle physics, it works on Aristotelian principles; but as to things own component parts, I said EXTERNAL location in my original post for a reason. Yu Shan and Autochthonia can have space WITHIN themselves, existing as their own realms, but (other than Gateways or Seal-Breach portals) they have no external spatial relationship to anywhere else. Hence being &quot;Elsewhere&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T19:57:47-07:00","id":1121158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Childofthesun1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1121156#post1121156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And esoteric bullshit infuriates me because it seems like a futile exercise in illogic committed by stoners. &quot;Like, what if nothing was a thing. And what if everything only existed because nothing, like, makes everything exist, maaan?&quot; That makes no sense. I'm cool with the Wyld vomiting forth twisted, howling monstrosities and the landscape shifting in nightmarish and hostile ways, that's fine. &quot;Up is down&quot; is comprehensible. &quot;Up is glurple&quot; is incomprehensible and is neither entertaining for me to read nor feasible to play.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem that the Shinma aren't usable in play is fair. They have their place in underlining the themes of the Raksha and how their relationship to their Graces and the Wyld works, but 2nd Edition definitely started making too big a deal out of them. It didn't help that the relevant writer of Graceful Wicked Mask didn't understand the point Dr Moran was making with set theory, and made Advaita Iraivan its own Shinma, when the entire point of &quot;God&quot; being an aspect of Nirguna is that a Prime Mover is one of the things that defines the Exalted-setting BY NOT EXISTING.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T21:52:22-07:00","id":1121188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Childofthesun1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1121156#post1121156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And esoteric bullshit infuriates me because it seems like a futile exercise in illogic committed by stoners. &quot;Like, what if nothing was a thing. And what if everything only existed because nothing, like, makes everything exist, maaan?&quot; That makes no sense. I'm cool with the Wyld vomiting forth twisted, howling monstrosities and the landscape shifting in nightmarish and hostile ways, that's fine. &quot;Up is down&quot; is comprehensible. &quot;Up is glurple&quot; is incomprehensible and is neither entertaining for me to read nor feasible to play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I am sure that is exactly how it happened. The resemblance to the kabbalistic notions of Ayin, Ein Sof, and the emanation of being out of nothingness is obviously a coincidence. I mean real religious scholars never uttered lines like:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> AYIN means No-Thing. AYIN is beyond Existence, separate from any-thing. AYIN is Absolute Nothing. AYIN is not above or below. Neither is AYIN still or in motion. There is nowhere where AYIN is, for AYIN is not. AYIN is soundless, but neither is it silence. Nor is AYIN a void - and yet out of the zero of AYIN'S no-thingness comes the one of EIN SOF </div> </div> </div>or<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the same manner that the abstract clothes itself in the perceptible, so also measureless eternity clothes itself in a fixed time, and eternal indivisible, infinite essences clothe themselves in defined, finite, and divisible units - the ayin clothes itself the the yesh. </div> </div> </div>A discussion of the set theory exercise they were getting at: <a href=\"http://nobilis.me/quotes:neph-talks-set-theory\" target=\"_blank\">http://nobilis.me/quotes:neph-talks-set-theory</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 07-27-2017, 12:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T22:35:29-07:00","id":1121198,"title":"","content":"I once had a player in one of my games equate Elsewhere with &quot;out of my metaphysical ass&quot; .<br /> <br /> After the laughter died down (and I stopped imagining George Carlin trying to explain the concept of Elsewhere, which only lead to more laughter) it occurred to me that it boils down to being defined as &quot;irrelevant&quot;. It's a bit like how, in some video games and movies, you don't see the character's weapon stowed until they are drawing it for battle. See also: Looney Tunes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3976-silent-witness","name":"Silent Witness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3976_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T04:07:42-07:00","id":1121250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1121188#post1121188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, I am sure that is exactly how it happened. The resemblance to the kabbalistic notions of Ayin, Ein Sof, and the emanation of being out of nothingness is obviously a coincidence. I mean real religious scholars never uttered lines like:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> or<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> A discussion of the set theory exercise they were getting at: <a href=\"http://nobilis.me/quotes:neph-talks-set-theory\" target=\"_blank\">http://nobilis.me/quotes:neph-talks-set-theory</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously such discussion has been part of religious traditions. Obviously it has held some value there as part of mysticism and philosophy. There it's still pretty incomprehensible, but at least it's doing so to get you to think or create enlightenment. But in a tabletop game, I seriously question its usefulness. It really strikes me as being for campaign background only, and the only value I see is in putting the ST in proper mindset to run the Deep Wyld.<br /> <br /> It's like, I signed up for Exalted to play demigods' epic struggle to bend the world to their will, or less eloquently, to punch gods in the face. How did I even get here?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T04:35:10-07:00","id":1121255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Childofthesun1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1121250#post1121250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Obviously such discussion has been part of religious traditions. Obviously it has held some value there as part of mysticism and philosophy. There it's still pretty incomprehensible, but at least it's doing so to get you to think or create enlightenment. But in a tabletop game, I seriously question its usefulness. It really strikes me as being for campaign background only, and the only value I see is in putting the ST in proper mindset to run the Deep Wyld.<br /> <br /> It's like, I signed up for Exalted to play demigods' epic struggle to bend the world to their will, or less eloquently, to punch gods in the face. How did I even get here?</div> </div> </div> </div>Exalted: come for the epic anime fight scenes and wondrous occult imagery, stay for the intricate metaphysical analysis and interesting pre-industrial sociopolitical commentary!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ultimate Jade-Screened Exalted Scholar, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304239-my-next-campaign-tdhr-peach\" target=\"_blank\">THDR : Future Dragon-Blooded campaign</a>, and other links.<br /> If you like Ex3, you can support <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/holdenshearer\" target=\"_blank\">Holden</a> on Patreon!","edited":{"userid":541,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","user":"LeTipex","date":". 07-28-2017, 05:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","name":"LeTipex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T05:51:36-07:00","id":1121273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LeTipex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1121255#post1121255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exalted: come for the epic anime fight scenes and wondrous occult imagery, stay for the intricate metaphysical analysis and interesting pre-industrial sociopolitic commentary!</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, that was brilliant. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T02:04:33-07:00","id":1121754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Silent Witness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1116730-solars-starting-the-game-with-artifacts?p=1121198#post1121198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I once had a player in one of my games equate Elsewhere with &quot;out of my metaphysical ass&quot; .<br /> <br /> After the laughter died down (and I stopped imagining George Carlin trying to explain the concept of Elsewhere, which only lead to more laughter) it occurred to me that it boils down to being defined as &quot;irrelevant&quot;. It's a bit like how, in some video games and movies, you don't see the character's weapon stowed until they are drawing it for battle. See also: Looney Tunes.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bOr &quot;Hammer Space&quot; in many anime shows where an annoyed female character pull some implausible weapon out of nowhere to clobber the often clueless male character vexing her. That actually does sound like Exalted when you think about it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T13:37:16-07:00","id":1122041,"title":"","content":"I don't know, I guess I always thought of sending something to Elsewhere as translating the object into the essential <i>idea</i> of the thing with one's magic, and then translating it back into a physical object when needed. Rather than floating in a parallel dimension that has spatial coordinates and such, it's more just a potentiality associated with the exalt that they can make real with an act of will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T13:42:23-07:00","id":1122042,"title":"","content":"I'd honestly prefer that, but it doesn't completely work because of realms like Yu Shan and Autochthonia being referred to as being Elsewhere as well. So things Elsewhere have to still fully exist. But as I said, I don't think of it as a big vacuum with spatial coordinates, but rather as each thing or place Elsewhere as existing independently without spatial relationship to anything or other place beyond themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}